#. ja: ドードー
#. de: Dodo
#. fr: dodo
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: These large, flightless cloudkin originated from the island of Mazlaya, and were brought to the mainland by Qiqirn who bred them for their eggs. The free races of Eorzea have reared the rotund creatures ever since, though they are now valued primarily for their meat. Would-be poultry farmers be warned: when seeking to defend itself, a dodo will spit forth a sleep-inducing secretion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:1:0:0"
msgid "Dodo"
msgstr "Додо"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Dodos
#. fr: dodos
#. column 0: Dodo
#. column 8: These large, flightless cloudkin originated from the island of Mazlaya, and were brought to the mainland by Qiqirn who bred them for their eggs. The free races of Eorzea have reared the rotund creatures ever since, though they are now valued primarily for their meat. Would-be poultry farmers be warned: when seeking to defend itself, a dodo will spit forth a sleep-inducing secretion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:1:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: マズラヤ島を原産地とする飛翔力のない大型鳥。丸々としており胸肉は特に美味。採卵のためにキキルン族が大陸に持ち込み、今ではエオルゼアの諸都市でも広く飼養されている。防衛のため口から催眠性の分泌物を噴出する。
#. de: Diese flugunfähigen Riesenvögel stammen ursprünglich von der Insel Mazlaya und wurden von den Qiqirn ihrer Eier wegen auf den Kontinent gebracht. Seither werden die rundlichen Kreaturen von den Völkern Eorzeas überall gezüchtet, heutzutage werden sie jedoch hauptsächlich wegen ihres Fleisches geschätzt. Ein Wort der Warnung: Dodos sind in der Lage, ein Schlaf-induzierendes Sekret auf ihre Gegner zu spucken.
#. fr: D'abord introduits depuis l'île de Mazlaya pour leurs œufs par des Qiqirns, ces gros oiseaux incapables de voler sont désormais élevés par les Éorzéens pour leur délicieuse chair. Attention toutefois, un dodo crachera une substance soporifique s'il se sent menacé<nbsp>!
#. column 0: Dodo
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:1:0:8"
msgid "These large, flightless cloudkin originated from the island of Mazlaya, and were brought to the mainland by Qiqirn who bred them for their eggs. The free races of Eorzea have reared the rotund creatures ever since, though they are now valued primarily for their meat. Would-be poultry farmers be warned: when seeking to defend itself, a dodo will spit forth a sleep-inducing secretion."
msgstr "Эти крупные нелетающие птицы родом с острова Мазлая. Кикирн привезли их на материк, чтобы разводить ради яиц. С тех пор их выращивают по всей Эорзее, хотя теперь ценят главным образом за мясо. Будущим птицеводам на заметку: защищаясь, додо плюётся усыпляющим секретом."

#. ja: トンベリ
#. de: Tomberry
#. fr: tomberry
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Little is known about this inscrutable race of manlike creatures that inhabits the ruins of Nym─a culture that reached its peak during the Fifth Astral Era. Tonberries wear clothing and are adept in the use of complex tools, both of which would seem to suggest a civilized level of intelligence. Recently discovered texts from Nymian times suggest that the green denizens of the Wanderer's Palace are the carriers of a terrible pestilence.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:2:0:0"
msgid "Tonberry"
msgstr "Тонберри"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Tomberrys
#. fr: tomberrys
#. column 0: Tonberry
#. column 8: Little is known about this inscrutable race of manlike creatures that inhabits the ruins of Nym─a culture that reached its peak during the Fifth Astral Era. Tonberries wear clothing and are adept in the use of complex tools, both of which would seem to suggest a civilized level of intelligence. Recently discovered texts from Nymian times suggest that the green denizens of the Wanderer's Palace are the carriers of a terrible pestilence.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:2:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 第五星暦時代に栄えた「ニーム」文明の遺跡内に棲む謎多き民。人のように衣服を着用し、道具も器用に扱うことから知性は高いと思われる。ニーム時代の石板には、「病魔の運び手」などの不吉な記述が見られるという。
#. de: Es ist nur wenig bekannt über dieses rätselhafte Volk, das in einer Tempelruine aus der Zeit Nyms lebt, einer Kultur, die ihre Hochzeit während der Fünften Ära des Lichts hatte. Tomberrys tragen Kleidung und sind in der Lage, komplexe Werkzeuge zu benutzen, beides Merkmale für einen gewissen Zivilisiertheitsgrad. Kürzlich entdeckte Texte aus alten Zeiten weisen darauf hin, dass die grünen Bewohner des Palastes des Wanderers Träger einer schrecklichen Seuche sind.
#. fr: On sait peu de choses sur ces créatures qui hantent les ruines de Nym, une cité qui a connu son apogée à la 5e ère astrale, mais leurs vêtements et leurs outils laissent supposer qu'elles sont intelligentes. De vieilles tablettes de pierre indiqueraient que les tomberrys sont porteurs d'une terrible maladie.
#. column 0: Tonberry
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:2:0:8"
msgid "Little is known about this inscrutable race of manlike creatures that inhabits the ruins of Nym─a culture that reached its peak during the Fifth Astral Era. Tonberries wear clothing and are adept in the use of complex tools, both of which would seem to suggest a civilized level of intelligence. Recently discovered texts from Nymian times suggest that the green denizens of the Wanderer's Palace are the carriers of a terrible pestilence."
msgstr "Об этой загадочной расе человекоподобных существ, обитающей в руинах Нима, почти ничего не известно. Нимская цивилизация достигла расцвета в Пятую астральную эру. Тонберри носят одежду и умело обращаются со сложными инструментами — похоже, разумом они не обделены. Недавно найденные тексты нимской эпохи утверждают, что зелёные обитатели Дворца скитальца разносят страшную заразу."

#. ja: サボテンダー
#. de: Sabotender
#. fr: pampa
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Found exclusively in arid regions, cactuars are known for their ability to survive extended periods under the scorching sun on naught but the moisture stored within their bodies. Conditioned by the brutal nature of their surroundings, cactuars are quick to defend themselves, launching a barrage of needle-like projectiles at potential predators─and the occasional unwary traveler.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:3:0:0"
msgid "Sabotender"
msgstr "Саботендер"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Sabotender
#. fr: pampas
#. column 0: Sabotender
#. column 8: Found exclusively in arid regions, cactuars are known for their ability to survive extended periods under the scorching sun on naught but the moisture stored within their bodies. Conditioned by the brutal nature of their surroundings, cactuars are quick to defend themselves, launching a barrage of needle-like projectiles at potential predators─and the occasional unwary traveler.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:3:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 乾燥地帯に生息する移動性のサボテン。体内に水分を溜め込むことで、長期間の乾燥に耐えることで知られる。また、過酷な環境を生き残るため、捕食者と認めた相手には幹内に潜む針を発射。積極的な防衛行動をとる。
#. de: Sabotender sind aus<shy>schließ<shy>lich in trockenen Gebieten aufzufinden und sind dafür bekannt, sich selbst bei brütender Hitze wohlzufühlen. Sie können ausreichend Feuchtigkeit in ihren Körpern speichern, um selbst unter widrigsten Bedingungen überleben zu können. Diese Umstände haben sie außerdem so konditioniert, dass sie sich verteidigen können, indem sie nadelartige Projektile auf Raubtiere - oder auf unbedachte Reisende - abfeuern.
#. fr: S'étant adaptés pour survivre à leur habitat aride et dangereux, ces cactus ambulants ont la faculté de conserver de l'humidité dans leur organisme et peuvent se défendre d'éventuels prédateurs en lançant une multitude d'épines douloureuses.
#. column 0: Sabotender
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:3:0:8"
msgid "Found exclusively in arid regions, cactuars are known for their ability to survive extended periods under the scorching sun on naught but the moisture stored within their bodies. Conditioned by the brutal nature of their surroundings, cactuars are quick to defend themselves, launching a barrage of needle-like projectiles at potential predators─and the occasional unwary traveler."
msgstr "Кактусники обитают только в засушливых краях и могут долго выдерживать палящее солнце, довольствуясь влагой, запасённой в теле. Суровая жизнь закалила их: почуяв угрозу, они обстреливают врага иглами — будь то хищник или зазевавшийся путник."

#. ja: スプリガン
#. de: Spriggan
#. fr: spriggan
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Spriggans are neither sprites nor faeries, but share similarities with both. They are known to inhabit rocky regions and the deep recesses of mines. These black-furred soulkin are famous for carrying a gem or chunk of ore about with them at all times─a custom which may explain the popularly held belief within the mining fraternity that they are bringers of good fortune. Their classification as soulkin is based on a theory expounded in the Codex of Stone, which asserts that the creatures are naught but vessels for the will of the earth.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:4:0:0"
msgid "Spriggan"
msgstr "Спригган"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Spriggans
#. fr: spriggans
#. column 0: Spriggan
#. column 8: Spriggans are neither sprites nor faeries, but share similarities with both. They are known to inhabit rocky regions and the deep recesses of mines. These black-furred soulkin are famous for carrying a gem or chunk of ore about with them at all times─a custom which may explain the popularly held belief within the mining fraternity that they are bringers of good fortune. Their classification as soulkin is based on a theory expounded in the Codex of Stone, which asserts that the creatures are naught but vessels for the will of the earth.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:4:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 岩場や鉱山に出没する漆黒の魔物。常に貴石を大切に持ち歩いているため｢財宝の守護者｣と呼ばれ、採掘師に敬われている。呪具綱とされる理由は｢彼らは石に操られているに過ぎない｣とする古典『百石大鑑』の分類による。
#. de: Spriggans bewohnen felsige Regionen und tiefe Höhlen. Diese schwarzen Fellkreaturen sind bekannt dafür, stets wertvolle Steine und Minerale bei sich zu tragen - eine Angewohnheit, die ihnen bei Minenarbeitern einen Ruf als Glücksbringer eingebracht hat. Ihre Klassifizierung als Arkane geht auf eine Theorie im Kodex der Steine zurück, die besagt, dass diese Kreaturen nichts weiter als Botschafter für den Willen der Erde sind.
#. fr: Ces créatures que l'on rencontre dans les grottes et les carrières d'Éorzéa semblent toujours avoir des pierres précieuses sur elles, si bien que les mineurs pensent qu'elles portent chance. Si le Codex des pierres les classifie comme arcanas, c'est parce que les spriggans ne seraient que le vaisseau de la volonté de la terre.
#. column 0: Spriggan
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:4:0:8"
msgid "Spriggans are neither sprites nor faeries, but share similarities with both. They are known to inhabit rocky regions and the deep recesses of mines. These black-furred soulkin are famous for carrying a gem or chunk of ore about with them at all times─a custom which may explain the popularly held belief within the mining fraternity that they are bringers of good fortune. Their classification as soulkin is based on a theory expounded in the Codex of Stone, which asserts that the creatures are naught but vessels for the will of the earth."
msgstr "Спригганы — не духи и не феи, хотя чем-то напоминают и тех и других. Они селятся в скалистых местах и глубоко в шахтах. Эти черношёрстные духи камня всегда носят с собой самоцвет или кусок руды. Возможно, поэтому рудокопы считают их приносящими удачу. К духам камня спригганов причисляют согласно теории из «Кодекса камня»: они — лишь сосуды, исполняющие волю земли."

#. ja: プリン
#. de: Pudding
#. fr: pudding
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: These gelatinous creatures spawn in the agglomerations of residual matter that sometimes form in the void. Though able to mimic rudimentary sounds of speech in order to draw forth their prey, they are not thought to be especially intelligent beings. As a relatively low-ranked voidsent, flans occupy the tenth rung of the hierarchy.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:5:0:0"
msgid "Pudding"
msgstr "Пудинг"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Puddings
#. fr: puddings
#. column 0: Pudding
#. column 8: These gelatinous creatures spawn in the agglomerations of residual matter that sometimes form in the void. Though able to mimic rudimentary sounds of speech in order to draw forth their prey, they are not thought to be especially intelligent beings. As a relatively low-ranked voidsent, flans occupy the tenth rung of the hierarchy.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:5:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 異界ヴォイドの汚水がたまる沼地で生まれた異形の魔物。獲物をおびき寄せるために人の声色をまねることがあるが、知性は低い。妖異学者たちの分類でも、妖異十二階位の第十位とされており、下級の妖異といえるだろう。
#. de: Diese gallertartigen Kreaturen sind Verdichtungen von Materierückständen aus dem Nichts. Obwohl sie in der Lage sind, rudimentäre Sprechgeräusche zu imitieren, um ihre Beute anzulocken, gelten sie nicht als sonderlich intelligente Wesen. Puddings gehören zu den rangniederen Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ten, sie haben den zehnten Rang innerhalb der Hierarchie inne.
#. fr: Ces êtres gélatineux proviennent de l'agglomération de résidus issus du néant. Bien que capables d'imiter des voix humaines pour attirer des proies, ils ne semblent pas être par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>rement in<shy>tel<shy>li<shy>gents et se placent au dixième rang parmi les douze que compte la Hiérarchie du néant.
#. column 0: Pudding
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:5:0:8"
msgid "These gelatinous creatures spawn in the agglomerations of residual matter that sometimes form in the void. Though able to mimic rudimentary sounds of speech in order to draw forth their prey, they are not thought to be especially intelligent beings. As a relatively low-ranked voidsent, flans occupy the tenth rung of the hierarchy."
msgstr "Эти студенистые существа рождаются из скоплений остаточной материи, которые порой образуются в Бездне. Чтобы выманить добычу, они подражают простым звукам речи, но особым умом, по-видимому, не отличаются. Среди исчадий Бездны они стоят на десятой ступени из двенадцати."

#. ja: ボム
#. de: Bomber
#. fr: bombo
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This barely contained sphere of volatile gas and flame occupies the eleventh rung of the voidsent's hierarchy of twelve. Bombs must replenish their internal reserves of fuel in order to survive, and are drawn to consume any source of oil or fat that they encounter, be it plant, animal, or man. Grenades, an even more explosive species of bomb, are a place higher in the hierarchy, standing upon the tenth rung.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:6:0:0"
msgid "Bomb"
msgstr "Бомба"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Bomber
#. fr: bombos
#. column 0: Bomb
#. column 8: This barely contained sphere of volatile gas and flame occupies the eleventh rung of the voidsent's hierarchy of twelve. Bombs must replenish their internal reserves of fuel in order to survive, and are drawn to consume any source of oil or fat that they encounter, be it plant, animal, or man. Grenades, an even more explosive species of bomb, are a place higher in the hierarchy, standing upon the tenth rung.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:6:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 妖異十二階位の第十一位にあたる火球状のガス生命体。人間を含む油脂分を有する動植物を見つけると、自身の燃料とするために見境なく襲いかかる。より高温の者は「グレネード」と呼ばれ、階位も第十位に位置付けられる。
#. de: Dieses Konglomerat aus flüchtigem Gas und Flammen hat den elften Rang der Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ten-Hierarchie inne. Bomber müssen ihre inneren Reserven auffrischen, um überleben zu können und stürzen sich daher auf jede potenzielle Quelle von Öl oder Fett, seien es Pflanzen, Tiere oder ein Vertreter der Sechs Völker. Besonders explosive Exemplare werden „Granaten“ genannt und rangieren eine Stufe höher in der Hierarchie.
#. fr: Appartenant au onzième rang de la Hiérarchie du néant, ces êtres composés de gaz et de feu ont besoin des huiles et graisses des végétaux, des animaux ou même des humains, afin de maintenir leur combustion. Les grenados sont une variété plus explosive et plus prépondérante.
#. column 0: Bomb
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:6:0:8"
msgid "This barely contained sphere of volatile gas and flame occupies the eleventh rung of the voidsent's hierarchy of twelve. Bombs must replenish their internal reserves of fuel in order to survive, and are drawn to consume any source of oil or fat that they encounter, be it plant, animal, or man. Grenades, an even more explosive species of bomb, are a place higher in the hierarchy, standing upon the tenth rung."
msgstr "Этот шар из летучего газа и пламени едва сдерживает собственный жар. Среди исчадий Бездны он занимает одиннадцатую ступень из двенадцати. Чтобы выжить, бомбам нужно пополнять запас топлива, поэтому они пожирают всё, в чём есть масло или жир: растения, животных и даже людей. Гранаты — ещё более взрывоопасная разновидность бомб — стоят ступенью выше, на десятой."

#. ja: マンドラゴラ
#. de: Mandragora
#. fr: mandragore
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The enigmatic mandragoras were first observed in the aftermath of the Seventh Umbral Era. It is not known whence they came, or if they even existed prior to the Calamity. Preliminary studies appear to suggest that the diminutive seedkin are sentient and capable of an advanced form of nonverbal communication, but further research is required to confirm these findings. The rest is mere speculation.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:7:0:0"
msgid "Mandragora"
msgstr "Мандрагора"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Mandragoras
#. fr: mandragores
#. column 0: Mandragora
#. column 8: The enigmatic mandragoras were first observed in the aftermath of the Seventh Umbral Era. It is not known whence they came, or if they even existed prior to the Calamity. Preliminary studies appear to suggest that the diminutive seedkin are sentient and capable of an advanced form of nonverbal communication, but further research is required to confirm these findings. The rest is mere speculation.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:7:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 第七霊災後に、忽然と姿を現した植物状生物。どこからやって来たのか、さっぱり解らない。どうやら知性らしきものがあるらしく、言語によらないコミュニケーション手段を持つらしいが、まだ研究の途上で詳細は不明である。
#. de: Die mysteriösen Mandragoras wurden zum ersten Mal in der Zeit nach der Siebten Katastrophe beobachtet. Über ihre Herkunft ist nichts bekannt, vorläufige Studien deuten jedoch darauf hin, dass die zierlichen Pflanzenwesen empfindungsfähige Kreaturen sind und zu einer hochentwickelten Form non-verbaler Kommunikation in der Lage sind. Erst weitere Forschung wird zeigen, ob sich diese Befunde verifizieren lassen.
#. fr: Les mys<shy>té<shy>rieu<shy>ses mandragores ont été observées pour la première fois après la 7e ère ombrale, mais nul ne sait si elles existaient avant le Fléau. Des études préliminaires suggèrent que ces créatures végétales seraient douées d'in<shy>tel<shy>li<shy>gence et posséderaient une forme avancée de communication non verbale.
#. column 0: Mandragora
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:7:0:8"
msgid "The enigmatic mandragoras were first observed in the aftermath of the Seventh Umbral Era. It is not known whence they came, or if they even existed prior to the Calamity. Preliminary studies appear to suggest that the diminutive seedkin are sentient and capable of an advanced form of nonverbal communication, but further research is required to confirm these findings. The rest is mere speculation."
msgstr "Загадочных мандрагор впервые заметили после Седьмой Умбральной эры. Неизвестно, откуда они появились и существовали ли вообще до Бедствия. Предварительные исследования показывают, что эти крошечные семенные создания разумны и способны к сложной невербальной коммуникации. Но это ещё предстоит подтвердить. Остальное — лишь догадки."

#. ja: コブラン
#. de: Kobalos
#. fr: coblyn
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The coblyn is a creature of startling appearance that skitters around on its tentacle-like appendages in search of ore. Gridanian scholars claim that a coblyn is an animal that fuses minerals to its body to create a defensive shell. Ul'dahn scholars dispute this theory, stating that these soulkin are, in fact, sentient clumps of geological matter that have adopted biological organs in order to facilitate propagation.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:8:0:0"
msgid "Coblyn"
msgstr "Коблин"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Kobalosse
#. fr: coblyns
#. column 0: Coblyn
#. column 8: The coblyn is a creature of startling appearance that skitters around on its tentacle-like appendages in search of ore. Gridanian scholars claim that a coblyn is an animal that fuses minerals to its body to create a defensive shell. Ul'dahn scholars dispute this theory, stating that these soulkin are, in fact, sentient clumps of geological matter that have adopted biological organs in order to facilitate propagation.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:8:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 自らの殻を形成する鉱石を求めて這い回る奇妙な魔物。身を守るため背に鉱石を植え付けた動物とするグリダニアの学者と、増殖のために動物の器官を取り込んだ鉱石とするウルダハの学者とで、その解釈は分かれている。
#. de: Ein Kobalos, der auf der Suche nach nahrhaften Erzen auf seinen Tentakeln durch die Landschaft huscht, ist ein furchterregender Anblick. Gridanischen Gelehrten zufolge nutzen diese Tiere die Erze, um einen schützenden Panzer auf sich wachsen zu lassen. Gelehrte aus Ul'dah hingegen vertreten die Theorie, dass Kobalosse empfindungsfähige Klumpen aus geologischem Material sind, die biologische Organe entwickelt haben, um ihre Verbreitung zu begünstigen.
#. fr: Ces créatures d'apparence étonnante se déplacent sur leurs tentacules en quête de minerai. Selon les érudits gridaniens, il s'agirait d'animaux fusionnant la roche pour se créer une carapace. Cette théorie est réfutée à Ul'dah, où l'on considère que les coblyns sont plutôt des amas de matière géologique intelligent qui auraient développé des tissus biologiques.
#. column 0: Coblyn
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:8:0:8"
msgid "The coblyn is a creature of startling appearance that skitters around on its tentacle-like appendages in search of ore. Gridanian scholars claim that a coblyn is an animal that fuses minerals to its body to create a defensive shell. Ul'dahn scholars dispute this theory, stating that these soulkin are, in fact, sentient clumps of geological matter that have adopted biological organs in order to facilitate propagation."
msgstr "Коблины — удивительные существа, которые снуют на щупальцеподобных конечностях в поисках руды. Учёные Гридании считают их животными, покрывающими тело минералами для защиты. Учёные Ульды с ними не согласны: по их мнению, это разумные сгустки геологической материи, обзаведшиеся биологическими органами для размножения."

#. ja: モルボル
#. de: Morbol
#. fr: morbol
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The morbol is a terrible beast that moves upon its slime-covered vines and roots. Highly aggressive, it kills both animals and plants with a combination of its noxious breath and ceaselessly flailing tendrils. Upon occasion, the beast will also emit a sweet-smelling gas which induces a deep sleep. Rather than rending or chewing, the fang-shaped thorns which line the morbol's maw serve to hold prey immobile during digestion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:9:0:0"
msgid "Morbol"
msgstr "Морбол"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Morbol
#. fr: morbols
#. column 0: Morbol
#. column 8: The morbol is a terrible beast that moves upon its slime-covered vines and roots. Highly aggressive, it kills both animals and plants with a combination of its noxious breath and ceaselessly flailing tendrils. Upon occasion, the beast will also emit a sweet-smelling gas which induces a deep sleep. Rather than rending or chewing, the fang-shaped thorns which line the morbol's maw serve to hold prey immobile during digestion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:9:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 巻きひげを使って這い回る移動性の大型食獣植物。獲物を誘引するため、また気絶させるために強烈な甘い香りを捕食器官から放つ。多数の牙状の棘は、獲物を噛み砕くためではなく消化しきるまで捕らえておくためにある。
#. de: Morbol sind furchterregende Bestien, die sich mithilfe ihrer Ranken und Wurzeln fortbewegen. Sie sind hochgradig aggressiv und töten mit einer Kombination aus ihrem giftigen Atem und den unaufhörlich herumfuchtelnden Ranken. Bisweilen versprühen die Bestien auch einen süßlich riechenden Duft, der ihre Gegner schlafen schickt. Statt ihre Beute mit den reißzahnähnlichen Dornen in ihrem Schlund zu zerfleischen, dienen diese lediglich dazu, die Beute ruhigzustellen, während sie verdaut wird.
#. fr: Se déplaçant sur leurs racines gluantes, ces horribles créatures végétales se montrent par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>rement agressives et dangereuses, tuant animaux et plantes grâce à une haleine putride et à des sarments puissants. Elles peuvent occasionnellement émettre un parfum doux et soporifique. Les crocs-épines qui garnissent leurs gueules servent à immobiliser leurs proies lors de la digestion.
#. column 0: Morbol
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:9:0:8"
msgid "The morbol is a terrible beast that moves upon its slime-covered vines and roots. Highly aggressive, it kills both animals and plants with a combination of its noxious breath and ceaselessly flailing tendrils. Upon occasion, the beast will also emit a sweet-smelling gas which induces a deep sleep. Rather than rending or chewing, the fang-shaped thorns which line the morbol's maw serve to hold prey immobile during digestion."
msgstr "Морбол — ужасное чудище, передвигающееся на покрытых слизью корнях и лозах. Он крайне агрессивен и убивает животных и растения ядовитым дыханием и непрестанно хлещущими щупальцами. Иногда морбол источает сладковатый усыпляющий газ. Зубчатые шипы в его пасти не разрывают и не пережёвывают добычу, а удерживают её, пока та переваривается."

#. ja: クァール
#. de: Coeurl
#. fr: coeurl
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Native to the regions of the Near East, these predatory quadrupeds are unrivaled in their savagery. A coeurl subdues its prey by unleashing electrical shocks from the two whip-like appendages that frame its fang-lined jaws. The feral specimens encountered in Eorzea descend from escaped war beasts once trained on a remote island at the mouth of the Rothlyt Sound known as the Pearl.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:10:0:0"
msgid "Coeurl"
msgstr "Куэрл"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Coeurl
#. fr: coeurls
#. column 0: Coeurl
#. column 8: Native to the regions of the Near East, these predatory quadrupeds are unrivaled in their savagery. A coeurl subdues its prey by unleashing electrical shocks from the two whip-like appendages that frame its fang-lined jaws. The feral specimens encountered in Eorzea descend from escaped war beasts once trained on a remote island at the mouth of the Rothlyt Sound known as the Pearl.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:10:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 類を見ない獰猛さで恐れられる四脚肉食獣。自在に動かすことができる二本の触角から、電撃を放ち獲物を麻痺させて捕食する。原産は近東地域。エオルゼアに生息するものは、戦闘用に持ち込まれた個体が野生化したもの。
#. de: Diese in den Gebieten des Nahen Ostens heimischen raubtierhaften Vierbeiner sind von unerreichter Wildheit. Ein Coeurl überwältigt seine Beute, indem er auf sie Elektroschocks von den peitschenartigen Fühlern an seinem Kiefer loslässt. Die ungezähmten Exemplare Eorzeas stammen von entflohenen für den Krieg herangezüchteten Bestien ab, die einst auf einer abgeschiedenen Insel am Munde des Rothlyt-Meerbusen, auch bekannt als die Perle, trainiert wurden.
#. fr: Natifs du Proche-Orient, ces carnivores quadrupèdes capturent leurs proies en envoyant des décharges électriques avec les très longues moustaches qui ornent leur museau. Les spécimens sauvages que l'on trouve en Éorzéa descendraient de bêtes de combat échappées d'une île dans le golfe de Rothlyt.
#. column 0: Coeurl
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:10:0:8"
msgid "Native to the regions of the Near East, these predatory quadrupeds are unrivaled in their savagery. A coeurl subdues its prey by unleashing electrical shocks from the two whip-like appendages that frame its fang-lined jaws. The feral specimens encountered in Eorzea descend from escaped war beasts once trained on a remote island at the mouth of the Rothlyt Sound known as the Pearl."
msgstr "Эти хищные четвероногие родом с Ближнего Востока и славятся неукротимой свирепостью. Куэрл обездвиживает добычу электрическими разрядами, которые испускают два хлыстовидных отростка по обе стороны пасти, полной клыков. Дикие куэрлы Эорзеи ведут род от боевых зверей, сбежавших с отдалённого острова Жемчужина у входа в залив Ротлит."

#. ja: アーリマン
#. de: Ahriman
#. fr: ahriman
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Ahriman are a family of voidsent that manifest in the physical plane by investing their essences in the eyes of animals. They are possessed of great arcane ability, and fly by clawing their way along airborne currents of aether. According to studies of voidsent hierarchy, the ahriman family is of middling class, its various forms occupying the fourth and fifth rungs.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:11:0:0"
msgid "Ahriman"
msgstr "Ахриман"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Ahriman
#. fr: ahrimans
#. column 0: Ahriman
#. column 8: Ahriman are a family of voidsent that manifest in the physical plane by investing their essences in the eyes of animals. They are possessed of great arcane ability, and fly by clawing their way along airborne currents of aether. According to studies of voidsent hierarchy, the ahriman family is of middling class, its various forms occupying the fourth and fifth rungs.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:11:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 動物の眼球を依代にして、物質界に顕現する異界ヴォイド由来の魔物。高い魔力を有しており、空中のエーテルを掻いて浮遊。石化の術にも長けている。なお、妖異学の分類によれば、第四～五位程度の中級の存在とされる。
#. de: Ahriman gehören zu den Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ten und manifestieren sich in der materiellen Ebene, indem sie ihre Essenz in die Augen von Tieren einfließen lassen. Sie besitzen außer<shy>ordent<shy>liche arkane Fä<shy>hig<shy>kei<shy>ten und fliegen durch die Lüfte, indem sie sich an den Strömungen des Äthers festkrallen und daran entlanghangeln. Laut Studien über die Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ten sind Ahriman auf den mittleren Rängen vier und fünf angesiedelt.
#. fr: Les ahrimans sont des êtres du néant qui se manifestent dans le monde physique en enveloppant leur essence dans des yeux d'animaux. Ils possèdent de grandes capacités magiques et volent en s'agrippant aux courants éthéréens avec leurs griffes. Ces créatures de classe moyenne appartiendraient aux quatrième et cinquième rangs de la Hiérarchie du néant.
#. column 0: Ahriman
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:11:0:8"
msgid "Ahriman are a family of voidsent that manifest in the physical plane by investing their essences in the eyes of animals. They are possessed of great arcane ability, and fly by clawing their way along airborne currents of aether. According to studies of voidsent hierarchy, the ahriman family is of middling class, its various forms occupying the fourth and fifth rungs."
msgstr "Ахриманы — род исчадий Бездны, которые являются в материальный мир, вселяясь в глаза животных. Они обладают сильной магией и летают, цепляясь когтями за воздушные потоки эфира. Согласно исследованиям иерархии исчадий Бездны, ахриманы занимают средние ступени — четвёртую и пятую."

#. ja: グゥーブー
#. de: Goobbue
#. fr: goobbue
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: A goobbue is a lumbering beast that has a symbiotic relationship with the moss and lichen growing atop its head. This growth provides the creature with a measure of camouflage, and, in return, the goobbue keeps the vegetation moist during the drier seasons with water scooped up in its hands. Though seemingly placid, the goobbue is a relentless predator, snatching up anything that skitters or crawls and shoveling it into its cavernous mouth.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:12:0:0"
msgid "Goobbue"
msgstr "Губбу"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Goobbue
#. fr: goobbues
#. column 0: Goobbue
#. column 8: A goobbue is a lumbering beast that has a symbiotic relationship with the moss and lichen growing atop its head. This growth provides the creature with a measure of camouflage, and, in return, the goobbue keeps the vegetation moist during the drier seasons with water scooped up in its hands. Though seemingly placid, the goobbue is a relentless predator, snatching up anything that skitters or crawls and shoveling it into its cavernous mouth.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:12:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 小山のように巨大な二足獣。頭部に生える苔とは共生関係にあり、カモフラージュとする代わりに、乾期には長い手を使って保水を欠かさない。普段は動きが緩慢だが、空腹時には動くものを片っ端からその大口に放り込む。
#. de: Goobbue sind schwerfällige Kreaturen, die eine symbiotische Beziehung mit dem Moos und den Flechten, die auf ihrem Kopf wachsen, eingehen. Dieser Pflanzenwuchs beschert den Goobbue eine gewisse Tarnung und im Gegenzug spendieren die Goobbue den Pflanzen Feuchtigkeit während der trockeneren Jahreszeiten. Obwohl die Goobbue friedlich anmuten, sind sie unbarmherzige Jäger und schnappen sich alles, was über den Boden kreucht und fleucht, und schieben es sich in den riesigen Mund.
#. fr: Ces imposantes créatures ont une relation symbiotique avec la mousse et le lichen qui poussent sur leur tête, ces derniers offrant une forme de camouflage en échange d'un arrosage manuel pendant les saisons les plus sèches. Bien qu'ils aient l'air placide, les goobbues se révèlent des prédateurs implacables lorsqu'ils sont affamés.
#. column 0: Goobbue
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:12:0:8"
msgid "A goobbue is a lumbering beast that has a symbiotic relationship with the moss and lichen growing atop its head. This growth provides the creature with a measure of camouflage, and, in return, the goobbue keeps the vegetation moist during the drier seasons with water scooped up in its hands. Though seemingly placid, the goobbue is a relentless predator, snatching up anything that skitters or crawls and shoveling it into its cavernous mouth."
msgstr "Губбу — неповоротливый зверь, живущий в симбиозе с мхом и лишайником, растущими у него на голове. Растительность помогает ему маскироваться, а он в засушливые сезоны увлажняет её водой, зачерпнутой руками. Губбу кажется безобидным, но это неумолимый хищник: он хватает всё, что ползает или шныряет, и отправляет прямо в свою огромную пасть."

#. ja: チョコボ
#. de: Chocobo
#. fr: chocobo
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The domestication of chocobos in Eorzea appears to date back to prehistory, with ancient paintings recently discovered near Ishgard showing tribesfolk using the flightless yellow cloudkin to till the earth, transport grain, and carry warriors into battle. While the overwhelming majority of chocobos seen in Eorzea today are of Coerthan stock, it is rumored that wild breeds of the species─including those which have retained the capacity for flight─still thrive throughout forests nestled in the vastly unexplored valleys of Abalathia's Spine.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:13:0:0"
msgid "Chocobo"
msgstr "Чокобо"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Chocobos
#. fr: chocobos
#. column 0: Chocobo
#. column 8: The domestication of chocobos in Eorzea appears to date back to prehistory, with ancient paintings recently discovered near Ishgard showing tribesfolk using the flightless yellow cloudkin to till the earth, transport grain, and carry warriors into battle. While the overwhelming majority of chocobos seen in Eorzea today are of Coerthan stock, it is rumored that wild breeds of the species─including those which have retained the capacity for flight─still thrive throughout forests nestled in the vastly unexplored valleys of Abalathia's Spine.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:13:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 逞しい脚で大地を駆ける陸生の大型鳥。エオルゼアでは、古来より駄獣や輓獣、騎乗用途に用いられてきた。クルザスが一大生産地として知られるほか、アバラシア山脈の秘境「チョコボの森」には野生種も多いという。
#. de: Die Domestizierung der Chocobos in Eorzea geht vermeintlich auf prähistorische Zeiten zurück. Es existiert altes Bildmaterial, das Stammesangehörige dabei zeigt, wie sie die flugunfähigen Vögel dazu einsetzen, den Boden zu beackern und Krieger in den Kampf zu tragen. Auch wenn die große Mehrzahl von Chocobos in Eorzea von coerthischer Herkunft ist, wird gemunkelt, dass wilde Exemplare der Spezies - inklusive derer, die noch die Fähigkeit zu fliegen besitzen - in den unerforschten Wäldern von Abalathias Rückgrat leben.
#. fr: Ces grands oiseaux terrestres sont connus pour leur vélocité et sont utilisés comme bêtes de somme ou montures par les Éorzéens depuis les temps anciens. Le Coerthas est réputé être la principale région productrice de ces animaux, mais il existerait une forêt des chocobos dans les montagnes d'Abalathia, où vivrait un important troupeau de spécimens sauvages.
#. column 0: Chocobo
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:13:0:8"
msgid "The domestication of chocobos in Eorzea appears to date back to prehistory, with ancient paintings recently discovered near Ishgard showing tribesfolk using the flightless yellow cloudkin to till the earth, transport grain, and carry warriors into battle. While the overwhelming majority of chocobos seen in Eorzea today are of Coerthan stock, it is rumored that wild breeds of the species─including those which have retained the capacity for flight─still thrive throughout forests nestled in the vastly unexplored valleys of Abalathia's Spine."
msgstr "Эорзейцы приручили чокобо, похоже, ещё в доисторические времена. На древних рисунках, недавно найденных близ Ишгарда, изображены племена, которые использовали нелетающих жёлтых птиц, чтобы пахать землю, возить зерно и носить воинов в бой. Сегодня большинство эорзейских чокобо родом из Керта. Однако поговаривают, что дикие чокобо, в том числе сохранившие способность летать, до сих пор водятся в лесах неисследованных долин Хребта Абалатии."

#. ja: アマルジャ
#. de: Amalj'aa
#. fr: Amalj'aa
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The Amalj'aa are a race of nomadic beastmen who inhabit the grasslands of Paglth'an, where they subsist by hunting the native wildlife. They share a long and bitter history of conflict with the people of Ul'dah. Trained in the arts of war from a tender age, all members of an Amalj'aa clan, old and young, male and female, are skilled warriors. They also boast a fine mastery of metallurgy, and their weapons fetch a tidy sum from those seeking arms of quality.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:14:0:0"
msgid "Amalj'aa"
msgstr "Амалджа"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Amalj'aa
#. fr: Amalj'aa
#. column 0: Amalj'aa
#. column 8: The Amalj'aa are a race of nomadic beastmen who inhabit the grasslands of Paglth'an, where they subsist by hunting the native wildlife. They share a long and bitter history of conflict with the people of Ul'dah. Trained in the arts of war from a tender age, all members of an Amalj'aa clan, old and young, male and female, are skilled warriors. They also boast a fine mastery of metallurgy, and their weapons fetch a tidy sum from those seeking arms of quality.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:14:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: パガルザン草原で羊やトカゲを追いながら暮らす遊牧の民であり、ウルダハの宿敵。幼少より軍事調練を施され、老若男女すべてが優れた兵士である。また炎を操る冶金術に長け、彼らの作り出す武具は高値で取引される。
#. de: Der Wilde Stamm der Amalj'aa ist ein Volk von Nomaden, das das Grasland von Paglth'an durchstreift und sich dabei von der Jagd auf die heimische Fauna ernährt. Die Amalj'aa sind die Erzfeinde Ul'dahs. Alle Mitglieder eines Amalj'aa-Klans - egal, ob jung oder alt, ob Mann oder Frau - sind versierte Kämpfer, werden sie doch bereits im zarten Alter in den Kriegskünsten ausgebildet. Sie sind außerdem große Meister der Metallurgie, weshalb ihre Waffen bei denen hübsche Sümmchen erzielen, die Wert auf Qualität legen.
#. fr: Les Amalj'aa sont un peuple d'hommes-bêtes nomades originaires des prairies du Paglth'an, où ils vivent de la chasse d'animaux sauvages. Ennemis héréditaires d'Ul'dah, ils sont entraînés dans les arts de la guerre dès leur plus jeune âge, quel que soit leur sexe. Ils possèdent également une grande maîtrise de la métallurgie, leurs armes étant très appréciées des col<shy>lec<shy>tion<shy>neurs.
#. column 0: Amalj'aa
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:14:0:8"
msgid "The Amalj'aa are a race of nomadic beastmen who inhabit the grasslands of Paglth'an, where they subsist by hunting the native wildlife. They share a long and bitter history of conflict with the people of Ul'dah. Trained in the arts of war from a tender age, all members of an Amalj'aa clan, old and young, male and female, are skilled warriors. They also boast a fine mastery of metallurgy, and their weapons fetch a tidy sum from those seeking arms of quality."
msgstr "Амалджа — кочевой народ зверолюдей, населяющий луга Пагльт'ана и живущий охотой на местных зверей. Их история полна жестоких конфликтов с жителями Ульды. Военному делу амалджа обучают с малых лет, и каждый в клане — стар или млад, мужчина или женщина — умелый воин. Они также искусны в металлургии, и их оружие ценят те, кто ищет качественное снаряжение."

#. ja: イクサル
#. de: Ixal
#. fr: Ixal
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This aggressive mountain tribe claim the wind-blasted canyons of Xelphatol as their domain. Though their race has long since lost the capacity for flight, the feathered beastmen are fervently proud of their vestigial wings. The Ixal seek to reestablish their presence in the Black Shroud that they might once again fell trees in worship of their fickle deity─an ambition which places them at odds with the people of Gridania.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:15:0:0"
msgid "Ixal"
msgstr "Иксал"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Ixal
#. fr: Ixali
#. column 0: Ixal
#. column 8: This aggressive mountain tribe claim the wind-blasted canyons of Xelphatol as their domain. Though their race has long since lost the capacity for flight, the feathered beastmen are fervently proud of their vestigial wings. The Ixal seek to reestablish their presence in the Black Shroud that they might once again fell trees in worship of their fickle deity─an ambition which places them at odds with the people of Gridania.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:15:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 風の吹き荒ぶ大渓谷に住まう、好戦的な山岳の民。手に残る翼の痕跡は、大空を舞っていた証であり彼らの誇り。嵐神に木々を献じるため、かつて領していた黒衣森を取り戻さんと、グリダニアと激しく対立する。
#. de: Dieser Wilde Stamm beansprucht die durch Winderosion abgeschliffenen Canyons von Xelphatol für sich. Die Ixal haben längst die Fähigkeit zu fliegen verloren, dennoch sind die gefiederten Wilden stolz auf die rudimentären Flügel, die ihnen noch geblieben sind. Sie versuchen ihre Präsenz im Finsterwald wieder zu stärken, um eines Tages wieder Bäume fällen und ihrer launischen Gottheit huldigen zu können - ein Ziel, das die Bewohner Gridanias mit ihnen auf Kriegsfuß stehen lässt.
#. fr: Les Ixali sont une tribu agressive ayant pour domaine les ravins venteux de Xelphatol. Bien qu'ils ne soient plus capables de voler depuis longtemps, ces hommes-bêtes à plumes sont très fiers de leurs ailes atrophiées. Désireux de rétablir leur présence dans Sombrelinceul pour en exploiter les ressources sylvestres, ils sont en conflit avec les habitants de Gridania.
#. column 0: Ixal
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:15:0:8"
msgid "This aggressive mountain tribe claim the wind-blasted canyons of Xelphatol as their domain. Though their race has long since lost the capacity for flight, the feathered beastmen are fervently proud of their vestigial wings. The Ixal seek to reestablish their presence in the Black Shroud that they might once again fell trees in worship of their fickle deity─an ambition which places them at odds with the people of Gridania."
msgstr "Эта воинственная горная народность обитает в продуваемых ветрами каньонах Кселфатола. Пернатые зверолюды иксали давно утратили способность летать, но всё ещё гордятся остатками крыльев. Они стремятся вернуть себе Чёрную чащу, чтобы вновь рубить деревья в честь своего непостоянного божества. Из-за этого иксали и жители Гридании враждуют."

#. ja: 悪い子シルフ
#. de: Sylphe
#. fr: Sylphe
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Deep within the northeastern reaches of the Black Shroud live the reclusive sylphs. These diminutive beings resemble children's dolls wrapped in vibrant leaves. The demeanor of the sylphs is comparable to that of an innocent child, but their propensity to employ their magical talents to “playfully” torment travelers has all too often been the cause of untold anguish and even tragedy for their hapless victims.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:16:0:0"
msgid "Sylph"
msgstr "Сильф"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Sylphen
#. fr: Sylphes
#. column 0: Sylph
#. column 8: Deep within the northeastern reaches of the Black Shroud live the reclusive sylphs. These diminutive beings resemble children's dolls wrapped in vibrant leaves. The demeanor of the sylphs is comparable to that of an innocent child, but their propensity to employ their magical talents to “playfully” torment travelers has all too often been the cause of untold anguish and even tragedy for their hapless victims.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:16:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 黒衣森深くに住まう幽谷の民と呼ばれる小さな獣人。木の葉をまとった人形のような愛らしい姿をしている。優れた幻術の使い手が多いが、その術を用いて旅人を遭難させるなど、度を過ぎた悪戯が深刻な事態を招くことも。
#. de: Im nördlichen Gridania, in den Tiefen des Finsterwaldes, lebt zurückgezogen das Volk der Sylphen. Diese zierlichen Wesen ähneln Kinderpuppen, die man in strahlend grüne Blätter eingewickelt hat. Das Verhalten der Sylphen lässt sich dabei durchaus mit dem eines unschuldigen Kindes vergleichen, doch ihre Neigung, Gebrauch von ihren magischen Talenten zu machen, um Reisende zu triezen - wenn auch auf spielerische Weise - hat schon oft für Angst und Schrecken auf Seiten ihrer unglückseligen Opfer gesorgt.
#. fr: Dans les profondeurs de Sombrelinceul, au nord de Gridania, vit le peuple reclus des Sylphes. Malgré leur apparence de poupées vêtues de feuilles et leur com<shy>por<shy>te<shy>ment enfantin, ils n'hésitent pas à user de leur magie pour tourmenter malicieusement les voyageurs, causant nombre de traumatismes et de tragédies chez ceux qui ont eu le malheur de s'aventurer trop loin dans la forêt.
#. column 0: Sylph
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:16:0:8"
msgid "Deep within the northeastern reaches of the Black Shroud live the reclusive sylphs. These diminutive beings resemble children's dolls wrapped in vibrant leaves. The demeanor of the sylphs is comparable to that of an innocent child, but their propensity to employ their magical talents to “playfully” torment travelers has all too often been the cause of untold anguish and even tragedy for their hapless victims."
msgstr "В северо-восточной части Чёрной чащи, в самой её глубине, живут скрытные сильфы. Эти крошечные существа похожи на детские куклы, обёрнутые яркими листьями. По характеру они напоминают невинных детей, но часто используют свою магию, чтобы «шутки ради» мучить путников. Их проделки нередко оборачиваются для несчастных жертв тяжкими страданиями и даже трагедиями."

#. ja: コボルド
#. de: Kobold
#. fr: Kobold
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The kobolds are a race of mole-like creatures who have excavated a warren of tunnels under O'Ghomoro, a mountain situated in northern Vylbrand. Believing the ores of the earth to be a gift of the primal Titan, these subterranean beastmen seek to divine their deity's teachings through the arts of alchemy. The peace agreement forged between the kobolds and Limsa Lominsa has served little to quell resurgent hostilities.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:17:0:0"
msgid "Kobold"
msgstr "Кобольд"

