#. ja: アレンヴァルド・レンティヌス
#. de: Arenvald Lentinus
#. fr: Arenvald Lentinus
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “For a long time, I struggled to make sense of that day at the Waking Sands. Why I survived when A'aba and Aulie didn't. Not anymore.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:217:0:0"
msgid "Arenvald Lentinus"
msgstr "Аренвальд Лентинус"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Arenvald Lentinus
#. column 0: Arenvald Lentinus
#. column 8: “For a long time, I struggled to make sense of that day at the Waking Sands. Why I survived when A'aba and Aulie didn't. Not anymore.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:217:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「アバとオリ……俺を助けるために、<br>命を散らせた「暁」の仲間のためにも、<br>しっかり戦ってみせる」<br>暁の血盟：アレンヴァルド・レンティヌス
#. de: „Ich hab mich oft gefragt, warum ich den Überfall auf den Sonnenstein überlebt habe, aber A'aba und Aulie nicht. Jetzt weiß ich, dass Rhalgr andere Pläne für mich hat.“
#. fr: “Je me battrai de toutes mes forces... C'est le moins que je puisse faire pour honorer la mémoire de mes amis A'aba et Aulie, qui ont donné leur vie pour sauver la mienne.”
#. column 0: Arenvald Lentinus
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:217:0:8"
msgid "“For a long time, I struggled to make sense of that day at the Waking Sands. Why I survived when A'aba and Aulie didn't. Not anymore.”"
msgstr "«Долгое время я пытался понять, что произошло в тот день в Живых песках. Почему я выжил, а А'аба и Оли — нет. Теперь всё ясно»."

#. ja: 人狼族
#. de: Lupin
#. fr: Lupin
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This wolf-headed beast tribe has its origins on the continent of Othard. Known for their martial traditions, the Lupin became an integral part of Doman warfare after several of their clans pledged fealty to the region's warlords during their endless clash for supremacy. When the Empire seized control, however, many Lupin were conscripted into the imperial army and forced to fight abroad.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:218:0:0"
msgid "Lupin"
msgstr "Лупин"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Lupins
#. column 0: Lupin
#. column 8: This wolf-headed beast tribe has its origins on the continent of Othard. Known for their martial traditions, the Lupin became an integral part of Doman warfare after several of their clans pledged fealty to the region's warlords during their endless clash for supremacy. When the Empire seized control, however, many Lupin were conscripted into the imperial army and forced to fight abroad.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:218:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 東州オサード大陸にルーツを持つ狼頭の獣人種族。武の民として知られ、戦乱期に一部の部族が地方豪族と主従の契りを結んだことで、やがてドマの重要な構成員となった。帝国統治期に徴兵され、連れ去られた者も少なくない。
#. de: Diese Bestie mit dem Kopf eines Wolfes ist auf Othard heimisch. Die Lupin sind bekannt für ihre Kampfsporttraditionen und wurden ein wichtiger Bestandteil der domanischen Kriegsführung, da zahlreiche Stämme den örtlichen Kriegsherren bei ihrem endlosen Kampf um die Vorherrschaft ihre Gefolgschaft schworen. Als das Kaiserreich die Kontrolle übernahm, wurden viele Lupin in die garleische Armee eingezogen und gezwungen, in fernen Ländern zu kämpfen.
#. fr: Les Lupins sont originaires du continent oriental d'Othard et ont une morphologie proche de celle des humains, exception faite de leur tête de loup. Voyant en eux un peuple guerrier, les anciens seigneurs de Doma firent de leur sujet certains clans lupins durant les anciennes guerres intestines. Ces hommes-bêtes gagnèrent ainsi un statut social privilégié. Mal<shy>heu<shy>reu<shy>se<shy>ment, l'Empire reconnut chez eux ces mêmes qualités de combattants lors de leur conquête de Doma et les embrigada en nombre dans son armée.
#. column 0: Lupin
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:218:0:8"
msgid "This wolf-headed beast tribe has its origins on the continent of Othard. Known for their martial traditions, the Lupin became an integral part of Doman warfare after several of their clans pledged fealty to the region's warlords during their endless clash for supremacy. When the Empire seized control, however, many Lupin were conscripted into the imperial army and forced to fight abroad."
msgstr "Эта зверолюдская раса с волчьими головами родом с континента Отард. Лупины славятся воинскими традициями. Во время бесконечных войн за господство несколько их кланов присягнули местным военачальникам, и со временем лупины стали неотъемлемой частью армии Домы. Когда власть захватила Империя, многих лупинов насильно призвали в имперские войска и отправили воевать за пределами родины."

#. ja: ハンコック
#. de: Hancock
#. fr: Hancock
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “Once again, I must apologize. Too much time in the Far East, you see. One is compelled to talk in circles around everything here, and one finds oneself longing for the invigoratingly candid speech of the Ul'dahn markets.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:219:0:0"
msgid "Hancock"
msgstr "Хэнкок"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Hancock
#. column 0: Hancock
#. column 8: “Once again, I must apologize. Too much time in the Far East, you see. One is compelled to talk in circles around everything here, and one finds oneself longing for the invigoratingly candid speech of the Ul'dahn markets.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:219:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「失敬、失敬……<br>事を素早く正確にというウルダハ人気質……<br>この国でも嫌われがちな、私の悪癖なのデス……」<br>東アルデナード商会の番頭：ハンコック
#. de: „Wir Ul'dahner sind es nun mal gewohnt, die Dinge beim Namen zu nennen<nbsp>... Falls Euch meine freimütige Art gekränkt hat, bitte ich Euch vielmals um Entschuldigung.“
#. fr: “Je vous prie de bien vouloir m'en excuser... Ma devise est de toujours aller droit au but, car le temps, c'est de l'argent. Mais je dois bien avouer que parfois, mon honnêteté me coûte un peu...”
#. column 0: Hancock
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:219:0:8"
msgid "“Once again, I must apologize. Too much time in the Far East, you see. One is compelled to talk in circles around everything here, and one finds oneself longing for the invigoratingly candid speech of the Ul'dahn markets.”"
msgstr "«Прошу прощения, прошу прощения... Слишком долго я пробыл на Дальнем Востоке. Тут принято говорить вокруг да около, и я невольно тоскую по бодрой прямоте торговых рядов Ульды»."

#. ja: ヒスイ＆クレナイ
#. de: Hisui & Kurenai
#. fr: Hisui & Kurenai
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “To prove my point, here is a quick test for you─look very closely and tell me: am I Kurenai...or am I Hisui?”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:220:0:0"
msgid "Hisui & Kurenai"
msgstr "Хисуи и Курэнай"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Hisui & Kurenai
#. column 0: Hisui & Kurenai
#. column 8: “To prove my point, here is a quick test for you─look very closely and tell me: am I Kurenai...or am I Hisui?”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:220:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「ためしにお顔を近づけて、よく見てくださいまし。<br>私はクレナイでしょうか……<br>それともヒスイでしょうか？」<br>紅玉姫：クレナイ<br>クレナイの友：ヒスイ
#. de: „Tritt ruhig einen Schritt näher und sieh dir mein Gesicht genau an. Na, bin ich Kurenai oder vielleicht doch Hisui?“
#. fr: “Vous pouvez vous approcher si vous voulez regarder de plus près, vous savez<nbsp>! Dites-moi juste à qui vous pensez avoir affaire. Kurenai... ou Hisui<nbsp>?”
#. column 0: Hisui & Kurenai
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:220:0:8"
msgid "“To prove my point, here is a quick test for you─look very closely and tell me: am I Kurenai...or am I Hisui?”"
msgstr "«Для проверки подойдите поближе и хорошенько присмотритесь. Кто перед вами: Курэнай... или Хисуи?»"

#. ja: ワニュウドウ＆カタシャリン
#. de: Wanyudo & Katasharin
#. fr: wanyûdô & katasharin
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: A mammet-type construction prevalent in the Far East. The cartwheels, adorned with the unsettling faces of a man and woman, are said to resemble mythical apparitions known for stealing the souls of any who look upon them─a design deliberately intended to frighten away cowardly interlopers.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:221:0:0"
msgid "Wanyudo & Katasharin"
msgstr "Ванюдо и Катасарин"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: wanyûdô & katasharin
#. column 0: Wanyudo & Katasharin
#. column 8: A mammet-type construction prevalent in the Far East. The cartwheels, adorned with the unsettling faces of a man and woman, are said to resemble mythical apparitions known for stealing the souls of any who look upon them─a design deliberately intended to frighten away cowardly interlopers.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:221:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 東方地域で造られる一種の魔法人形。牛車の車輪に、男女の顔を模した面が付いた奇妙な姿をしているのは、当地に伝わる「見る者の魂を奪う怪異」の伝承を再現しているため。不法侵入者を恐れさせる狙いがあるようだ。
#. de: Diese schaurig-seltsamen Dämonenbildnisse aus der Folklore des Fernen Ostens sind typischerweise auf Radnarben von Ochsenkarren dargestellt. Der Sage nach soll ihr Anblick dem Betrachter seine Seele entreißen. Für gewöhnlich dienen sie zur Abschreckung von abergläubischen Dieben.
#. fr: Ces automates nés en Orient s'apparentent à des roues de charrette sur lesquelles on aurait greffé des visages d'homme ou de femme, un ornement pour le moins dérangeant qui fait écho à la légende selon laquelle ces masques auraient le pouvoir de déposséder de leur âme ceux qui les regardent. De quoi décourager bien des intrus...
#. column 0: Wanyudo & Katasharin
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:221:0:8"
msgid "A mammet-type construction prevalent in the Far East. The cartwheels, adorned with the unsettling faces of a man and woman, are said to resemble mythical apparitions known for stealing the souls of any who look upon them─a design deliberately intended to frighten away cowardly interlopers."
msgstr "Разновидность магических кукол, распространённая на Дальнем Востоке. Колёса повозок с жуткими лицами мужчины и женщины напоминают призраков из легенд: будто те крадут души всякого, кто на них взглянет. Их нарочно создавали, чтобы отпугивать трусливых незваных гостей."

#. ja: ハタモト
#. de: Hatamoto
#. fr: hatamoto
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The spirit of an armored warrior who died in battle. The hatamoto are a class of soldier in Hingashi who often fought as personal guards for the nobility during the Age of Blood. Great numbers of these loyal vassals perished on the battlefield, and their battered, armor-clad forms are sometimes still spotted wandering the land in search of elusive victory.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:222:0:0"
msgid "Hatamoto"
msgstr "Хатамото"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: hatamoto
#. column 0: Hatamoto
#. column 8: The spirit of an armored warrior who died in battle. The hatamoto are a class of soldier in Hingashi who often fought as personal guards for the nobility during the Age of Blood. Great numbers of these loyal vassals perished on the battlefield, and their battered, armor-clad forms are sometimes still spotted wandering the land in search of elusive victory.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:222:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 討ち死にした鎧武者の死霊。本来、旗本とはひんがしの国における武士階級のひとつで、戦乱の時代には豪族たちの近衛兵として戦うことが多かった。そのため、戦場で死することも多く、東方地域では鎧姿の亡者が散見されるようだ。
#. de: Der Geist eines gefallenen Samurai in voller Rüstung. „Hatamoto“ ist in Hingashi die Bezeichnung für den Rang eines Samurai, der in der Zeit der Kriegswirren als Leibwächter eines Familienclans diente. In den zahlreichen Schlachten zahlten die Hatamoto einen hohen Blutzoll, weswegen sie nicht selten als untote in voller Montur dargestellt werden.
#. fr: Le spectre d'un valeureux samouraï tombé au champ d'honneur. On désignait autrefois par <i>hatamoto</i> les guerriers d'un certain rang, souvent des protecteurs de riches familles seigneuriales. Leur destin était dans la majorité des cas de mourir au combat, et ceux dont l'âme n'a pu trouver le repos hantent encore les terres orientales de nos jours.
#. column 0: Hatamoto
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:222:0:8"
msgid "The spirit of an armored warrior who died in battle. The hatamoto are a class of soldier in Hingashi who often fought as personal guards for the nobility during the Age of Blood. Great numbers of these loyal vassals perished on the battlefield, and their battered, armor-clad forms are sometimes still spotted wandering the land in search of elusive victory."
msgstr "Дух облачённого в доспехи воина, павшего в бою. В Хингаси хатамото — особый класс воинов, которые в Эпоху Крови часто служили телохранителями знати. Множество верных вассалов погибло на поле брани, и теперь их израненные фигуры в доспехах порой бродят по земле в поисках недостижимой победы."

#. ja: ユキンコ
#. de: Flöckchen
#. fr: yukinko
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: A close relative of the korpokkur, the yukinko cover themselves with a pointed hat of grass stalks to protect themselves from the cold and the falling snow. Known as “wintering,” this behavior has been mimicked by Far Eastern gardeners as a means of sheltering their own vulnerable trees and shrubs from the elements.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:223:0:0"
msgid "Yukinko"
msgstr "Юкинко"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Flöckchen
#. fr: yukinko
#. column 0: Yukinko
#. column 8: A close relative of the korpokkur, the yukinko cover themselves with a pointed hat of grass stalks to protect themselves from the cold and the falling snow. Known as “wintering,” this behavior has been mimicked by Far Eastern gardeners as a means of sheltering their own vulnerable trees and shrubs from the elements.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:223:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: コロポックルの近縁種。イネ科の植物の茎を集め、自らに覆いかぶせることで積雪や冷気から身を護る。この行動は「冬囲い」と呼ばれている。ちなみに、東方地域ではこのユキンコの習性を真似て、樹木を守る造園技術が発展した。
#. de: Die Flöckchen sind nahe Verwandte der Korpokkur. Mit den Stängeln von Süßgräsern fertigen sie sich einen schützenden Umhang gegen den Schnee und die Kälte in Pagos. Die Gewohnheit der Flöckchen hat im Osten übrigens Gärtner dazu inspiriert, Pflanzen und Bäume auf ähnliche Art überwintern zu lassen.
#. fr: Ces animaux sont des cousins des korpokkur qui ramassent des tiges de paille pour con<shy>fec<shy>tion<shy>ner des capes ru<shy>di<shy>men<shy>taires leur permettant de résister au froid et à la neige. Les Orientaux les imitent d'ailleurs depuis longtemps et ont perfectionné cette technique en inventant les voiles d'hivernage qui protègent leurs arbres par temps glacial.
#. column 0: Yukinko
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:223:0:8"
msgid "A close relative of the korpokkur, the yukinko cover themselves with a pointed hat of grass stalks to protect themselves from the cold and the falling snow. Known as “wintering,” this behavior has been mimicked by Far Eastern gardeners as a means of sheltering their own vulnerable trees and shrubs from the elements."
msgstr "Близкие родичи корпоккура, юкинко укрываются остроконечными шапками из травяных стеблей, спасаясь от холода и снега. Это поведение называют «зимовкой». Садовники Дальнего Востока переняли этот способ, чтобы укрывать от непогоды уязвимые деревья и кустарники."

#. ja: セイテンタイセイ
#. de: Qitian Dasheng
#. fr: Qitian Dasheng
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: As with others of its ilk, this simian auspice gained divine might after enduring a millennium of life. Qitian Dasheng, whose name means “Great Sage, Heaven's Equal,” dwelled in the Swallow's Compass to prevent his master's creation─the tamate-bako of geomancy─from falling into unscrupulous hands.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:224:0:0"
msgid "Qitian Dasheng"
msgstr "Цитянь Дашэн"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Qitian Dasheng
#. column 0: Qitian Dasheng
#. column 8: As with others of its ilk, this simian auspice gained divine might after enduring a millennium of life. Qitian Dasheng, whose name means “Great Sage, Heaven's Equal,” dwelled in the Swallow's Compass to prevent his master's creation─the tamate-bako of geomancy─from falling into unscrupulous hands.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:224:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 千年の時を生きたことで、神通力を得た猿の瑞獣。師が創った時を操る神器「風水玉手箱」を、悪しき者の手より守るため、ガンエン廟の周辺で暮らしていた。なお、その名は「天にも等しき大聖者」を意味する一種の称号である。
#. de: Seit seinem tausendsten Lebensjahr ist dieser Affe ein Zuiju. Um die Schatulle der rinnenden Zeit, die sein Meister einst schuf, vor den falschen Händen zu schützen, verschanzte er sich mit ihr im Kompass der Schwalbe. Sein Name bedeutet so viel wie Heiliger, der dem Himmel gleicht.
#. fr: Ce singe s'est métamorphosé en Zuijû et a acquis un immense pouvoir après avoir vécu plus de mille ans. Il monte la garde au Compas de l'Hirondelle, afin que le fûsui-tamatebako, un ancien artefact manipulant le temps et créé par son maître, ne tombe pas entre de mauvaises mains. On l'appelle aussi “Grand Sage, l'Égal du Ciel”.
#. column 0: Qitian Dasheng
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:224:0:8"
msgid "As with others of its ilk, this simian auspice gained divine might after enduring a millennium of life. Qitian Dasheng, whose name means “Great Sage, Heaven's Equal,” dwelled in the Swallow's Compass to prevent his master's creation─the tamate-bako of geomancy─from falling into unscrupulous hands."
msgstr "Как и другие подобные существа, эта обезьяна обрела божественную силу, прожив тысячу лет. Цитянь Дашэн — «Великий мудрец, равный Небу» — жил у Компаса Ласточки, чтобы творение своего мастера, фэншуй-шкатулку, не прибрали к рукам недобрые люди."

#. ja: ヒルコ
#. de: Hiruko
#. fr: Hiruko
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: An adversary faced on the thirtieth floor of Heaven-on-High. Standing as a challenge for those heroes who would battle against threats of cataclysmic proportions, Hiruko was created through forbidden arts now lost to the world.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:225:0:0"
msgid "Hiruko"
msgstr "Хируко"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Hiruko
#. column 0: Hiruko
#. column 8: An adversary faced on the thirtieth floor of Heaven-on-High. Standing as a challenge for those heroes who would battle against threats of cataclysmic proportions, Hiruko was created through forbidden arts now lost to the world.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:225:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: アメノミハシラの30層で戦うことになる存在。霊災規模の災厄に対抗し得る英雄を育てるため、その候補となる人材を試すために立ちはだかる。どうやら、その生成には今や失われた、禁忌の技術が用いられているようだ。
#. de: Hiruko ist der Wächter der dreißigsten Ebene der Himmelssäule. Seine Aufgabe ist es, alle Helden zu prüfen und jenen Abenteurer zu finden, der die nächste Katastrophe zu verhindern vermag. Es heißt, er beherrscht eine Reihe geheimer, längst vergessener Techniken.
#. fr: Cette mystérieuse entité barre la route aux braves qui parviennent à se hisser au trentième étage du Pilier des Cieux. Conçue pour ne laisser passer que les héros qui ont un espoir de survie face à des cataclysmes de l'envergure des fléaux, elle remplit sa mission d'écrémage en s'appuyant sur un arsenal conséquent, constitué de sortilèges interdits et aujourd'hui disparus.
#. column 0: Hiruko
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:225:0:8"
msgid "An adversary faced on the thirtieth floor of Heaven-on-High. Standing as a challenge for those heroes who would battle against threats of cataclysmic proportions, Hiruko was created through forbidden arts now lost to the world."
msgstr "Противник, с которым сталкиваются на тридцатом этаже Высоких небес. Хируко создан запретным искусством, ныне утраченным, и служит испытанием для героев, которым предстоит сразиться с угрозами масштаба бедствия."

#. ja: しあわせうさぎ
#. de: Glückshase
#. fr: lapin du bonheur
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: As the name implies, this small, curious creature is rumored to bring fortune wherever it goes. Upon taking a liking to someone─the requisite for which is not understood─the bunny will lead this favored individual to the location of hidden treasures. Participants in the Eureka field investigations have reported several sightings of the beasts, but little else is known about their habits or life cycle.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:226:0:0"
msgid "Happy Bunny"
msgstr "Счастливый кролик"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Glückshasen
#. fr: lapins du bonheur
#. column 0: Happy Bunny
#. column 8: As the name implies, this small, curious creature is rumored to bring fortune wherever it goes. Upon taking a liking to someone─the requisite for which is not understood─the bunny will lead this favored individual to the location of hidden treasures. Participants in the Eureka field investigations have reported several sightings of the beasts, but little else is known about their habits or life cycle.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:226:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 幸せを運ぶと噂される奇妙な小動物。いかなる基準かはわからないが、気に入った者を財宝の在り処へと導くらしい。エウレカの調査に参加した者たちの間で、何件かの目撃情報が寄せられているが、その生態には謎が多い。
#. de: Ein wundersames, kleines Geschöpf, das jene, die es in sein Herz schließt, zu einem Schatz führen soll. Was man tun muss, um die Gunst des Glückshasen zu gewinnen, ist dabei nicht ganz klar. Bei den Mitgliedern der Eureka-Expedition ist das Tier deshalb Gesprächsthema Nummer Eins.
#. fr: Ces mystérieux petits animaux sont connus pour porter chance sur Eurêka. L'équipe d'exploration a reçu plusieurs rapports d'aventuriers clamant que les lapins s'attacheraient parfois à eux et les guideraient vers des caches aux trésors. Personne ne sait en revanche comment s'attirer leur bénédiction à coup sûr.
#. column 0: Happy Bunny
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:226:0:8"
msgid "As the name implies, this small, curious creature is rumored to bring fortune wherever it goes. Upon taking a liking to someone─the requisite for which is not understood─the bunny will lead this favored individual to the location of hidden treasures. Participants in the Eureka field investigations have reported several sightings of the beasts, but little else is known about their habits or life cycle."
msgstr "Как подсказывает название, это маленькое любопытное создание, по слухам, приносит удачу повсюду, где появляется. Если кролик проникнется к кому-либо симпатией — а как заслужить её, никому не известно, — он приведёт избранника к спрятанным сокровищам. Участники экспедиций по исследованию Эврики не раз встречали этих зверьков, однако об их повадках и жизненном цикле почти ничего не известно."

#. ja: ロウヒ
#. de: Louhi
#. fr: Louhi
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Encountered in the frozen wasteland of Pagos, this formidable voidsent employs its immense arcane strength to condense blades of ice from the surrounding aether. Scholars have yet to perform a comprehensive study, but the presence of numerous underlings suggest that in the voidsent hierarchy, Louhi holds at the very least the rank of lesser noble.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:227:0:0"
msgid "Louhi"
msgstr "Лоухи"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Louhi
#. column 0: Louhi
#. column 8: Encountered in the frozen wasteland of Pagos, this formidable voidsent employs its immense arcane strength to condense blades of ice from the surrounding aether. Scholars have yet to perform a comprehensive study, but the presence of numerous underlings suggest that in the voidsent hierarchy, Louhi holds at the very least the rank of lesser noble.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:227:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 寒冷地パゴス帯にて確認された大型妖異。膨大な魔力を活かして環境エーテルを束ね、氷の刃を作り出して武装している。妖異学者による研究が待たれるが、多数の配下を率いていることからも、下級貴族級以上の存在と思われる。
#. de: Ein mächtiger Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ter, der in Pagos auf Eureka gesichtet wurde. Mit seinen gewaltigen arkanen Kräften bündelt er den Äther in seiner Umgebung und schafft daraus eine eisige Klinge. Ein abschließendes Ergebnis steht noch aus, aber Nichtsforscher glauben, es mit einem höheren Adelswesen zu tun zu haben. Die Tatsache, dass Louhi zahlreiche Untergebene um sich schart, scheint dies zu bestätigen.
#. fr: Découverte à Eurêka Pagos, cette imposante démone manie une paire de lames de glace qu'elle matérialise en manipulant l'énergie éthérée environnante. Si la communauté scien<shy>ti<shy>fi<shy>que ne s'est pas encore penchée sur son cas, sa capacité à contrôler de nombreux serviteurs indique qu'elle occupe un rang élevé dans la hiérarchie des démons.
#. column 0: Louhi
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:227:0:8"
msgid "Encountered in the frozen wasteland of Pagos, this formidable voidsent employs its immense arcane strength to condense blades of ice from the surrounding aether. Scholars have yet to perform a comprehensive study, but the presence of numerous underlings suggest that in the voidsent hierarchy, Louhi holds at the very least the rank of lesser noble."
msgstr "Этого грозного демона встретили в ледяной пустоши Пагоса. Огромная магическая сила позволяет ему сгущать эфир вокруг себя и создавать ледяные клинки. Учёные ещё не провели подробного исследования, но множество прислужников наводит на мысль, что в иерархии демонов Лоухи занимает как минимум низший дворянский ранг."

#. ja: ツクヨミ
#. de: Tsukuyomi
#. fr: Tsukuyomi
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This primal manifested in Doma, the result of a summoning fueled by a Red Kojin relic and a trove of Empire-supplied crystals. In certain legends, Tsukuyomi is revered as the Lady of the Moon─the most common tales surrounding this figure, however, depict the entity as male.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:228:0:0"
msgid "Tsukuyomi"
msgstr "Цукуёми"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Tsukuyomi
#. column 0: Tsukuyomi
#. column 8: This primal manifested in Doma, the result of a summoning fueled by a Red Kojin relic and a trove of Empire-supplied crystals. In certain legends, Tsukuyomi is revered as the Lady of the Moon─the most common tales surrounding this figure, however, depict the entity as male.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:228:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: ドマに降臨した蛮神。帝国軍が紅甲羅のコウジン族から手に入れた神器「白銅鏡」の力によって、召喚が行われた。なお、東方の伝承によれば、ツクヨミは夜と月を統べる神とされているが、一般的には男性の姿で描かれることが多い。
#. de: Ein Primae, den die Garlear in Doma mithilfe eines magischen Spiegels der Rotpanzer beschworen. In Legenden ist Tsukuyomi die Herrscherin des Mondes und der Nacht, wird jedoch oft in männlicher Gestalt dargestellt.
#. fr: Cette Primordiale s'est manifestée en grande partie grâce au pouvoir du Masokagami, un trésor sacré que l'Empire s'est procuré auprès des Kojin rouges. On l'appelle la Maîtresse de la lune et de la nuit, et bien qu'elle apparût sous forme féminine lors de son invocation à Doma, cette divinité est généralement représentée sous les traits d'un homme dans la culture orientale.
#. column 0: Tsukuyomi
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:228:0:8"
msgid "This primal manifested in Doma, the result of a summoning fueled by a Red Kojin relic and a trove of Empire-supplied crystals. In certain legends, Tsukuyomi is revered as the Lady of the Moon─the most common tales surrounding this figure, however, depict the entity as male."
msgstr "Этот праймал явился в Доме благодаря призыву, для которого использовали реликвию красных Кодзинов и целый запас имперских кристаллов. В некоторых сказаниях Цукуёми почитают как Владычицу Луны, хотя чаще всего это божество изображают мужчиной."

#. ja: 鬼龍ヤズマット
#. de: Yiasmat
#. fr: Yiazmat
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Little remains of former Dalmascan fusilier captain Ba'Gamnan, now twisted by the Duma into a soulless Lucavi who survives solely by drinking deep of the fallen Bangaa's deepest desires.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:229:0:0"
msgid "Yiazmat"
msgstr "Язмат"

