#. de: „Kweh, kweh!“
#. fr: “Kwééé... Kwé<nbsp>!”<br>- Nouvel employé des Forges de Garlond.
#. column 0: Alpha
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:247:0:8"
msgid "“Kweh...kweh!”"
msgstr "«Квээ... квэ!»"

#. ja: ナマキン大王
#. de: Majestät Goldbartel
#. fr: Altesse namazu nain doré
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: After learning that gold whisker dolls were popular in the Near East as talismans of good luck, this enterprising Namazu departed for Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han to indulge in a life of idle idolatry. He dyed his skin a gleaming metal hue, proclaimed himself the “Great Gold Whisker,” and succeeded in installing himself as the blessed kami guardian of a treasure vault.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:248:0:0"
msgid "Great Gold Whisker"
msgstr "Великий Золотой Ус"

#. ja: 0
#. de: NONE
#. fr: Altesse namazu nain doré
#. column 0: Great Gold Whisker
#. column 8: After learning that gold whisker dolls were popular in the Near East as talismans of good luck, this enterprising Namazu departed for Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han to indulge in a life of idle idolatry. He dyed his skin a gleaming metal hue, proclaimed himself the “Great Gold Whisker,” and succeeded in installing himself as the blessed kami guardian of a treasure vault.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:248:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 黄金色のナマズオ族。金色のナマキン人形が縁起物として、近東地域で人気だと知った彼は、働かずに生きていくためにラザハンへと渡航。錬金薬で全身を金色に変色させると「招福の神」を自称し、見事、宝物殿の守り神の地位を確立したのだった。
#. de: Goldener Namazuo. Im Wissen, dass sich Repliken der sogenannten Goldbarteln im Nahen Osten großer Beliebtheit als Glücksbringer erfreuen, beschloss er nach Radz-at-Han zu reisen, um dort ohne beschwerliche Arbeit ein Auskommen zu haben. Mittels einfacher Alchemie färbte er seinen gesamten Körper golden, um sich selbst zur Gottheit des Glücks auszurufen.  Auch gern als prächtige Wächtergottheit von Schatzkammern verwendet.
#. fr: Un Namazu de couleur or. Apprenant que les marionnettes dorées de Namazu étaient populaires comme porte-bonheur au Proche-Orient, il décida de se rendre à Radz-at-Han dans l'espoir de mener une vie de farniente. Il changea la couleur de son corps en doré grâce à une potion alchimique et réussit à s'arroger un rôle de divinité protectrice de la salle des trésors.
#. column 0: Great Gold Whisker
#. column 2: 0
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:248:0:8"
msgid "After learning that gold whisker dolls were popular in the Near East as talismans of good luck, this enterprising Namazu departed for Radz<hyphen>at<hyphen>Han to indulge in a life of idle idolatry. He dyed his skin a gleaming metal hue, proclaimed himself the “Great Gold Whisker,” and succeeded in installing himself as the blessed kami guardian of a treasure vault."
msgstr "Узнав, что на Ближнем Востоке золотые фигурки намацу считаются талисманами на удачу, этот предприимчивый намацу отправился в Радз-ат-Хан, чтобы жить в своё удовольствие и не работать. Он окрасил кожу в блестящий металлический цвет, объявил себя «Великим Золотым Усом» и сумел стать божественным стражем сокровищницы."

