#. ja: 複製サレタ工場廃墟にて遭遇した存在。黒い装束に身を包んだ少年のように見えるが、その正体は人を模して作られた自動歩兵人形、アンドロイドなのだという。機械生命体を操っていたが、その目的などは定かではない。
#. de: Auf den ersten Blick schien 9S ein Junge in schwarzer Kleidung zu sein, doch er entpuppte sich als ein künstliches Konstrukt aus der kopierten Fabrik, als ein Androide. Der Androide manipulierte Maschinenwesen, doch bisher ist nicht klar, zu welchem Zweck.
#. fr: Ce jeune garçon vêtu de noir rencontré dans la réplique de l'usine désaffectée a tout d'un enfant normal, mais sous cette apparence se cacherait en réalité un androïde que n'a d'humain que son aspect physique. En outre, personne ne sait pourquoi il contrôlait une forme de vie mécanique...
#. column 0: 9S
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:282:0:8"
msgid "A child encountered in the Copied Factory. Appearing as a young boy clad in black garb, it is in fact an android─an advanced machine designed in imitation of mankind. 9S was witnessed to be controlling machine lifeforms within the factory, though to what end it remains unknown."
msgstr "В Копии фабрики встретили ребёнка, похожего на мальчика в чёрной одежде. На деле это андроид — совершенная машина, созданная по образу человека. Видели, как 9S управлял находившимися на фабрике машинными формами жизни, но цель его действий неизвестна."

#. ja: フラワーバスケット
#. de: Blumenkorb
#. fr: panier fleuri
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: It is said these botanical beasts were originally golems created long ago in the Kingdom of Voeburt, conceived by mages to tend the royal gardens. Their present, floral appearance is the work of fae folk who settled there after the kingdom's fall, and indiscriminately bathed the land in pixie magicks. The result: beautiful flower beds as far as the eye can see, as well as a new breed of gardening guardians.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:283:0:0"
msgid "Flower Basket"
msgstr "Цветочная корзина"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Blumenkörbe
#. fr: paniers fleuris
#. column 0: Flower Basket
#. column 8: It is said these botanical beasts were originally golems created long ago in the Kingdom of Voeburt, conceived by mages to tend the royal gardens. Their present, floral appearance is the work of fae folk who settled there after the kingdom's fall, and indiscriminately bathed the land in pixie magicks. The result: beautiful flower beds as far as the eye can see, as well as a new breed of gardening guardians.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:283:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: かつてフッブート王国の魔道士たちが、牧草地の手入れを行わせるために創ったという一種のゴーレム。その生き残りをピクシーたちが、一帯を花畑に変えるために手を加えた結果、「動く花かご」のような姿になったらしい。
#. de: Einst waren diese Golems die Hüter und Pfleger voeburtschen Weidelands, von den alten Hofmagiern eigens zu diesem Zweck erschaffen. Ihr farbenfrohes Aussehen erhielten sie erst von den verspielten Pixies, die sie zu wandelnden Bouquets machten.
#. fr: Ces paniers animés étaient autrefois des golems créés par les mages voeburtois afin d'entretenir les pâturages du royaume. Les Pixies auraient usé de leur magie pour transformer ceux qui fonctionnaient encore après la disparition de leurs maîtres, tout cela afin qu'ils prennent soin de leurs si chers champs de fleurs.
#. column 0: Flower Basket
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:283:0:8"
msgid "It is said these botanical beasts were originally golems created long ago in the Kingdom of Voeburt, conceived by mages to tend the royal gardens. Their present, floral appearance is the work of fae folk who settled there after the kingdom's fall, and indiscriminately bathed the land in pixie magicks. The result: beautiful flower beds as far as the eye can see, as well as a new breed of gardening guardians."
msgstr "Говорят, давным-давно маги королевства Фоэбурт создали этих растительных чудищ из големов, чтобы те ухаживали за королевскими садами. После падения королевства там поселились феи и щедро оросили землю магией пикси. Так появились бескрайние цветочные поля и новые стражи садов — с цветочной внешностью."

#. ja: キタリ
#. de: Qitari
#. fr: Qitari
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: These rat-like people, once thought to be lost to time, were in truth living amidst the ruins of Ronka beneath the great falls in Rak'tika. Their average lifespan of a mere twenty-five summers is the reason for their meticulous recording of all they learn in life, that it may be passed on to future generations. The Ronkans too noted this predilection for recordkeeping, and so welcomed them as stewards in the royal court.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:284:0:0"
msgid "Qitari"
msgstr "Китари"

