#. ja: キタンナ神影洞に入り込んだことで、ロンカの盗掘者避けにかかり囚われていた巨大コウモリ。「光の氾濫」の無尽光によって目を焼かれた結果、聴覚が異様に発達、優れた反響定位能力と超音波を操る力を手に入れていたようだ。
#. de: Dieses Ungetüm von Fledermaus hütet die Irrungen der Qitari, dazu auserkoren, die heilige Stätte vor Räubern zu schützen. Sie verlor ihr schwaches Sehvermögen gänzlich an das gleißende Blenden der Lichtflut und verfeinerte über die Jahre ihren ohnehin schon ausgeprägten Ultraschallsinn.
#. fr: Cette gigantesque chauve-souris s'est autrefois retrouvée enfermée dans l'Enchevêtrement des Qitari et n'a cessé depuis de décourager les pillards. Ses yeux adaptés aux cavernes sombres ont été brûlés lors du déluge de Lumière, mais cela ne l'handicape pas outre mesure. En effet, elle perçoit la moindre vibration, et son ouïe redoutable lui permet de repérer ses proies par écholocalisation faisant d'elle un adversaire de taille.
#. column 0: Batsquatch
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:287:0:8"
msgid "A species of giant bat relocated to the Qitana Ravel to deter would-be thieves from trespassing in the ruins. In the searing Light of the Flood, their already limited eyesight was lost. By contrast, their already exceptional hearing and use of echolocation improved dramatically."
msgstr "Этот вид гигантских летучих мышей переселили в Равель Китаны, чтобы отпугивать расхитителей руин. Палящий Свет Потопа ослепил их, и без того плохо видевших. Зато их и прежде острый слух и способность к эхолокации невероятно развились."

#. ja: フォーギヴン・オブセニティー
#. de: Geläuterte Unzucht
#. fr: obscénité pardonnée
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Of the myriad sin eaters Lord Vauthry kept at his beck and call, this was said to be among his favorites. In another life, she was rumored to be a songstress of the Beehive who would ultimately find a higher calling at his side. One can but imagine how it came to be known by such a sinful moniker.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:288:0:0"
msgid "Forgiven Obscenity"
msgstr "Прощённая непристойность"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Geläuterte Unzüchtigkeiten
#. fr: obscénités pardonnées
#. column 0: Forgiven Obscenity
#. column 8: Of the myriad sin eaters Lord Vauthry kept at his beck and call, this was said to be among his favorites. In another life, she was rumored to be a songstress of the Beehive who would ultimately find a higher calling at his side. One can but imagine how it came to be known by such a sinful moniker.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:288:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: ドン・ヴァウスリー配下の上位罪喰い。その「素」となったのは、彼の情婦であったともビーハイヴの歌姫であったとも言われているが、真相は定かでない。前者の噂にちなみ、「オブセニティー（猥褻）」の罪を赦された者と呼ばれる。
#. de: Ein hochrangiger Sünden<shy>ver<shy>tilger, der keinem anderen gehorcht als Lord Vauthry persönlich. Vor ihrer Ver<shy>wand<shy>lung soll diese Kreatur die Primadonna des Lustspielhauses Bienenstock und angebliche Geliebte des Erlauchten Erlösers gewesen sein. Welch unzüchtiges Verhalten ihrem Namen Taufe stand, darüber wagen nicht einmal die gesprächigsten Klatschmäuler von Eulmore zu spekulieren.
#. fr: Un des plus puissants purgateurs que contrôlait don Vauthry. Certains pensent qu'il s'agissait autrefois d'une de ses maîtresses, d'autres d'une chanteuse à succès de La Ruche. Nul ne sait laquelle de ces origines est la vraie, mais la première pourrait expliquer son nom de purgateur.
#. column 0: Forgiven Obscenity
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:288:0:8"
msgid "Of the myriad sin eaters Lord Vauthry kept at his beck and call, this was said to be among his favorites. In another life, she was rumored to be a songstress of the Beehive who would ultimately find a higher calling at his side. One can but imagine how it came to be known by such a sinful moniker."
msgstr "Среди множества пожирателей грехов, которыми лорд Ваутри повелевал, этот считался одним из любимцев. Говорили, что прежде она пела в Пчелином улье, а затем обрела высокое призвание рядом с ним. Остаётся лишь гадать, почему она получила столь греховное имя."

#. ja: フアガス
#. de: Huaca
#. fr: Huaca
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: One of myriad beasts conjured by the great mages of the Ronkan Empire to keep watch of their holy temples. When dormant, they appear to be nothing more than ordinary statues, whose presence dominates the chambers in which they are placed. Intruders foolish enough to disturb the guardian's slumber will be forced to prove the measure of their worth, lest they be cast down into the darkest depths of the temple, never to be seen again.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:289:0:0"
msgid "Huaca"
msgstr "Уака"

