#. ja: 「よっこいニャ……っと……。<br>ふぅ……、これで準備よしですニャー」<br>猫型魔法人形：ねこみみさん
#. de: „Schwing dich in die Hängematte, gönn dir eine Kokosnussmilch und lass die Seele ordentlich baumeln!“
#. fr: “Et hop... Fiou... Et voilà, le terrain est prêt<nbsp>!”
#. column 0: Felicitous Furball
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:370:0:8"
msgid "“Ugh, my poor back... Goodness, I'm due for a healthy amount of grease after that ordeal.”"
msgstr "«Ох, спина-то как ноет... Ну и выдался денёк! Теперь бы не помешало как следует смазать суставы»"

#. ja: アンデン
#. de: Anden
#. fr: Anden
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “If I had hands, I'd give myself a smart rap on the head to get the blood flowing. ...Or sap flowing, as it were.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:371:0:0"
msgid "Anden"
msgstr "Анден"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Anden
#. fr: Anden
#. column 0: Anden
#. column 8: “If I had hands, I'd give myself a smart rap on the head to get the blood flowing. ...Or sap flowing, as it were.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:371:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「う～～ん、頭を叩いて刺激を与えてみる……？<br>いや、今の俺には手がないから、叩いてもらうしかないね！？」<br>しゃべる草人：アンデン
#. de: „Ja genau, vielleicht hilft ein kräftiger Schlag auf die Baumkrone<nbsp>...? Ah, aber ich habe keine Arme, also müsste jemand anderes ran<nbsp>...“
#. fr: “Hum... Et si je me donnais un bon coup sur le crâne...<nbsp>? Quoique, sans mains, ça risque d'être difficile...”
#. column 0: Anden
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:371:0:8"
msgid "“If I had hands, I'd give myself a smart rap on the head to get the blood flowing. ...Or sap flowing, as it were.”"
msgstr "«Вот бы мне руки — стукнул бы себя по макушке, чтобы кровь разогнать... Хотя, в моём случае, скорее сок. Но рук-то нет, придётся кого-нибудь попросить!»"

#. ja: スーパールゲイエ
#. de: Suprae-Lugae
#. fr: Super Lugae
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Despite engineering himself into a twisted amalgamation of flesh and metal, this magitek inventor was bested by an adventurer in the Tower of Babil. Further misfortune left him as a head without a body─thus did he contrive to attach his gleaming skull to the hulking remains of Barnabas, his “beautiful little boy,” and maximize his offensive capabilities.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:372:0:0"
msgid "Suprae-Lugae"
msgstr "Супраэ-Лугаэ"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Suprae-Lugae
#. fr: Super Lugae
#. column 0: Suprae-Lugae
#. column 8: Despite engineering himself into a twisted amalgamation of flesh and metal, this magitek inventor was bested by an adventurer in the Tower of Babil. Further misfortune left him as a head without a body─thus did he contrive to attach his gleaming skull to the hulking remains of Barnabas, his “beautiful little boy,” and maximize his offensive capabilities.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:372:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 魔導技師ルゲイエの成れの果て。機械化を果たすも冒険者に敗北、さらになんやかんやあって頭部だけになってしまった後、愛すべき息子、バルナバの身体とドッキング。ルゲイエを超えるルゲイエとなったのである。
#. de: Dass er sich in eine unheilige Kreatur aus Metall und Fleisch verwandelte, hat diesen Magitek-Ingenieur nicht davor bewahrt, im Turm von Babil von einem kühnen Abenteurer besiegt zu werden. Gewisse Umstände trennten seinen Kopf von seinem Körper, doch fand sein Haupt ein neues Zuhause auf den Schultern von Barnabas, seinem „geliebten Sohn“.
#. fr: Malgré la mécanisation de son propre corps, l'ingénieur magitek Lugae s'est retrouvé vaincu par <if $gn4>une aventurière<else>un aventurier</if>  dans la tour de Babil. Après avoir perdu tout son corps en dehors de sa tête, il s'amarre à son fils adoré, Barnabas, surpassant ainsi celui qu'il était précédemment.
#. column 0: Suprae-Lugae
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:372:0:8"
msgid "Despite engineering himself into a twisted amalgamation of flesh and metal, this magitek inventor was bested by an adventurer in the Tower of Babil. Further misfortune left him as a head without a body─thus did he contrive to attach his gleaming skull to the hulking remains of Barnabas, his “beautiful little boy,” and maximize his offensive capabilities."
msgstr "Несмотря на то что этот изобретатель магитека превратил себя в жуткую смесь плоти и металла, его одолел искатель приключений в Башне Вавил. А после новых несчастий от него осталась одна голова. Тогда он ухитрился приладить свой блестящий череп к огромному телу Барнаба, своего «милого мальчика», и тем самым усилить боевые возможности."

#. ja: ガンカナグー
#. de: Gancanagh
#. fr: Gancanagh
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This anthropoid mandragora modified by aetherochemical experimentation was cultivated to be a charismatic leader to its troops. Too charismatic, perhaps, as its enhanced intelligence inspired it to devise a revolution against its overlords, which led to its subsequent banishment to Eureka Orthos for purposes of “reeducation.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:373:0:0"
msgid "Gancanagh"
msgstr "Ганканах"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Gancanagh
#. fr: Gancanagh
#. column 0: Gancanagh
#. column 8: This anthropoid mandragora modified by aetherochemical experimentation was cultivated to be a charismatic leader to its troops. Too charismatic, perhaps, as its enhanced intelligence inspired it to devise a revolution against its overlords, which led to its subsequent banishment to Eureka Orthos for purposes of “reeducation.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:373:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: マンドラゴラを魔科学的に改良したガルゲンメンライン種、その中でも部隊長として培養された個体。しかし、知能を向上させたせいか革命に賛同して反乱を企てたため、再教育のうえ、オルト・エウレカの警備に左遷されたらしい。
#. de: Ein Resultat von Experimenten, Spezien mithilfe der allagischen Technologie zu verbessern. Dieses Individuum basierte wohl ursprünglich auf einer Mandragora. Es wurde als Kommandant kultiviert, doch nach einer Umerziehung zur Bewachung von Eureka Orthos abgestellt<nbsp>- vielleicht aufgrund seiner hohen Intelligenz, vielleicht aufgrund seines Hangs zur Rebellion.
#. fr: Une mandragore de la famille des Solanacées améliorée magismologiquement. Ses capacités hors du commun lui ont permis de s'élever dans la hiérarchie de ses pairs, à tel point qu'elle chercha à se rebeller. Après reconditionnement, elle fut reléguée à la garde d'Eurêka Orthos.
#. column 0: Gancanagh
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:373:0:8"
msgid "This anthropoid mandragora modified by aetherochemical experimentation was cultivated to be a charismatic leader to its troops. Too charismatic, perhaps, as its enhanced intelligence inspired it to devise a revolution against its overlords, which led to its subsequent banishment to Eureka Orthos for purposes of “reeducation.”"
msgstr "Эту человекоподобную мандрагору изменили с помощью эфирохимических экспериментов и вырастили, чтобы она стала харизматичным командиром. Возможно, слишком харизматичным: обретя высокий интеллект, она задумала восстание против хозяев. За это её сослали в Эврику-Ортос на «перевоспитание»."

#. ja: メネフィナ
#. de: Menphina
#. fr: Menphina
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The keeper of the twin moons and the goddess of love. Menphina commands the element of ice, and is often depicted as a maid carrying a round skillet. The large hound which appeared at her side in the phantom realm was a manifestation of Dalamud─the lesser moon known in legend as Menphina's loyal hound.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:374:0:0"
msgid "Menphina"
msgstr "Менфина"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Menphina
#. fr: Menphina
#. column 0: Menphina
#. column 8: The keeper of the twin moons and the goddess of love. Menphina commands the element of ice, and is often depicted as a maid carrying a round skillet. The large hound which appeared at her side in the phantom realm was a manifestation of Dalamud─the lesser moon known in legend as Menphina's loyal hound.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:374:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 双月と慈愛を司る女神。氷属の神力を有し、円い平鍋を持った健気な小間使いとして描かれることが多い。神域では大犬とともに顕現したが、これは、月の衛星ダラガブがメネフィナの番犬であると語られる伝承に由来するのだろう。
#. de: Menphina ist die Göttin des Mondes und der Liebe. Sie wird in der Kunst oft als tüchtiges Hausmädchen mit einer runden Pfanne dargestellt. Der große Hund, der an ihrer Seite im Schemenreich erschien, war eine Manifestation von Dalamud<nbsp>- der kleine Mond, der in den Legenden als Menphinas Wachhund erwähnt ist.
#. fr: Déesse de l'amour et gardienne des lunes jumelles. Elle commande l'élément glace et est communément représentée sous la forme d'une servante tenant une poêle à la main. Elle apparut aux côtés d'un gigantesque canidé à Omphalos, raison pour laquelle Dalamud est considéré comme son chien de garde.
#. column 0: Menphina
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:374:0:8"
msgid "The keeper of the twin moons and the goddess of love. Menphina commands the element of ice, and is often depicted as a maid carrying a round skillet. The large hound which appeared at her side in the phantom realm was a manifestation of Dalamud─the lesser moon known in legend as Menphina's loyal hound."
msgstr "Менфина — богиня любви и хранительница двух лун. Она повелевает стихией льда, и её часто изображают скромной служанкой с круглой сковородой в руках. В призрачном мире рядом с ней появился огромный пёс — воплощение Даламуда, малой луны, которую легенды называют верным псом Менфины."

#. ja: カイナッツォ
#. de: Cagnazzo
#. fr: Cagnazzo
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The archfiend of water, and one of Golbez's circle of four, Cagnazzo was pugnacious and warlike. He released a tide of voidsent into Garlemald through a voidgate in Lapis Manalis, and was later defeated at the hands of Eorzea's champion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:375:0:0"
msgid "Cagnazzo"
msgstr "Каньядзо"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Cagnazzo
#. fr: Cagnazzo
#. column 0: Cagnazzo
#. column 8: The archfiend of water, and one of Golbez's circle of four, Cagnazzo was pugnacious and warlike. He released a tide of voidsent into Garlemald through a voidgate in Lapis Manalis, and was later defeated at the hands of Eorzea's champion.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:375:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: ゴルベーザ四天王の一角たる水の大妖異。その言動には、戦いを好む荒々しさが見受けられる。ラピス・マナリスのヴォイドゲートから多数の妖異をガレマルドに差し向けたが、強者たる冒険者との死闘の末に消滅した。
#. de: Der Elementarfürst des Wassers und einer der vier Handlanger von Golbez. Cagnazzo war kriegerisch und schickte eine Horde Nichts<shy>gesand<shy>ter durch ein Portal in Lapis Manalis nach Garlemald. Ein Held aus Eorzea bereitete ihm ein unrühmliches Ende.
#. fr: L'un des quatre généraux de Golbez, aussi appelé le “maître de l'eau”, appréciant par<shy>ti<shy>cu<shy>liè<shy>rement les batailles. Il a envoyé de nombreuses créatures du néant depuis la porte du néant de Lapis Manalis, mais fut vaincu par <if $gn4>une aventurière<else>un aventurier</if>.
#. column 0: Cagnazzo
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:375:0:8"
msgid "The archfiend of water, and one of Golbez's circle of four, Cagnazzo was pugnacious and warlike. He released a tide of voidsent into Garlemald through a voidgate in Lapis Manalis, and was later defeated at the hands of Eorzea's champion."
msgstr "Каньядзо, водяной архизверь и один из четырёх приспешников Голбеза, был вспыльчив и воинственен. Через врата пустоты в Лапис Маналис он направил в Гарлемальд целый поток пустотников, но в конце концов пал от руки чемпиона Эорзеи."

#. ja: ルビカンテ
#. de: Rubicante
#. fr: Rubicante
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The archfiend of fire, and one of Golbez's circle of four. This intimidating warrior would pursue his goals with zealous abandon, conjuring hellish flames from the ashes of his own suffering in a bid to vanquish his foes.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:376:0:0"
msgid "Rubicante"
msgstr "Рубиканте"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Rubicante
#. fr: Rubicante
#. column 0: Rubicante
#. column 8: The archfiend of fire, and one of Golbez's circle of four. This intimidating warrior would pursue his goals with zealous abandon, conjuring hellish flames from the ashes of his own suffering in a bid to vanquish his foes.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:376:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: ゴルベーザ四天王の一角たる火の大妖異。威風堂々たる武人の佇まいと、目的のため身を焦がすことも厭わぬ狂熱の精神を併せ持つ。冒険者と対峙した際には、自身の心に潜む煉獄を具現し、その炎を引き出して戦ったという。
#. de: Der Elementarfürst des Feuers und einer der vier Handlanger von Golbez. Dieser Krieger war durch nichts einzuschüchtern und kommandierte höllische Flammen, geboren aus seinem eigenen Leid.
#. fr: L'un des quatre généraux de Golbez, aussi appelé le “maître du feu”. Ce guerrier redoutable n'hésiterait pas à se sacrifier pour accomplir son objectif. Lors de son combat contre <if $gn4>une aventurière<else>un aventurier</if>, il a invoqué de puissantes flammes sommeillant dans son propre cœur.
#. column 0: Rubicante
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:376:0:8"
msgid "The archfiend of fire, and one of Golbez's circle of four. This intimidating warrior would pursue his goals with zealous abandon, conjuring hellish flames from the ashes of his own suffering in a bid to vanquish his foes."
msgstr "Рубиканте — огненный архизверь и один из четырёх приспешников Голбеза. Этот грозный воин с фанатичным рвением шёл к своей цели, призывая адское пламя из пепла собственных страданий, чтобы сокрушить врагов."

#. ja: ヴェーネス
#. de: Venat
#. fr: Venat
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “And when mankind has found the strength to stand against despair, we shall silence the song of oblivion. She who sings it will learn our journey is far from over. This I promise.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:377:0:0"
msgid "Venat"
msgstr "Венат"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Venat
#. fr: Venat
#. column 0: Venat
#. column 8: “And when mankind has found the strength to stand against despair, we shall silence the song of oblivion. She who sings it will learn our journey is far from over. This I promise.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:377:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「人が、絶望に立ち向かえる強さを得たならば……<br>終焉を謳うものに、叩きつけにいきましょう。<br>人の答えを……私たちの旅は、終わるには惜しいものなのだと」<br>古きアゼム：ヴェーネス
#. de: „Wir werden das Lied vom Ende verstummen lassen. Die, die es singt, soll erfahren, dass unsere Reise noch längst nicht vorüber ist.“
#. fr: “Si l'humanité trouve en elle la force d'affronter le désespoir... alors nous pourrons remettre à sa place la chantre de l'ané<shy>an<shy>tis<shy>se<shy>ment. Il suffira de clamer haut et fort notre réponse. À quel point nous refusons que l'aventure s'arrête ici.”
#. column 0: Venat
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:377:0:8"
msgid "“And when mankind has found the strength to stand against despair, we shall silence the song of oblivion. She who sings it will learn our journey is far from over. This I promise.”"
msgstr "«Когда человечество обретёт силы противостоять отчаянию, мы заставим умолкнуть песнь забвения. Та, что поёт её, узнает: наш путь ещё далёк от завершения. Обещаю»"

#. ja: バケチョウチン
#. de: Kleiner Laternengeist
#. fr: bake-chôchin
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Rokkon's chochin were once a single lantern that had acquired a spirit after many years of use─and been summarily discarded by its fearful master. It sat patiently in Gorai's collection for a time, but when wickedness pervaded the temple, it divided itself into a multitude of mononoke, the better to devour men's souls as recompense for its abandonment.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:378:0:0"
msgid "Okuri Chochin"
msgstr "Окури тё:тин"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Kleine Laternengeister
#. fr: bake-chôchin
#. column 0: Okuri Chochin
#. column 8: Rokkon's chochin were once a single lantern that had acquired a spirit after many years of use─and been summarily discarded by its fearful master. It sat patiently in Gorai's collection for a time, but when wickedness pervaded the temple, it divided itself into a multitude of mononoke, the better to devour men's souls as recompense for its abandonment.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:378:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 長らく人に愛用されたことで霊性を獲得し、付喪神が宿った提灯。高僧ゴウライが集めた名品のひとつだったが、六根山の霊気にあてられて分裂、増殖したようだ。持ち主に捨てられた恨みから、人の魂を喰らおうとするらしい。
#. de: Ursprünglich war dieser Geist nur eine einfache Laterne. Doch aufgrund des Respekts und der Sorgfältigkeit, mit welcher ihre Besitzer sie über die Jahre hinweg behandelten, entwickelte sie ihr eigenes Bewusstsein.<br>Die mystischen Einflüsse des Rokkon führten allerdings zu der Spaltung und Vermehrung dieser Kreatur, welche nun, von dem Groll über ihren letzten Besitzer getrieben, das Verspeisen der Seelen von unglücklichen Abenteurern ihren Lebensinhalt nennt.
#. fr: Une ancienne lanterne qui appartenait autrefois à la collection du vieux moine Gôrai. Habitée par un esprit après avoir été abandonnée, la mystérieuse aura du mont Rokkon l'a fait se multiplier. Ses émules cherchent aujourd'hui à dévorer les âmes des humains pour se venger du sort qu'elle a subi.
#. column 0: Okuri Chochin
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:378:0:8"
msgid "Rokkon's chochin were once a single lantern that had acquired a spirit after many years of use─and been summarily discarded by its fearful master. It sat patiently in Gorai's collection for a time, but when wickedness pervaded the temple, it divided itself into a multitude of mononoke, the better to devour men's souls as recompense for its abandonment."
msgstr "Когда-то в Рокконе стоял один фонарь тё:тин, которому за долгие годы службы достался собственный дух. Испугавшись, хозяин просто выбросил его. Некоторое время фонарь терпеливо стоял в коллекции Горая, но, когда храм наполнился злобой, разделился на множество моногэ, чтобы пожирать людские души и отомстить за то, что его бросили."

#. ja: 鉄鼠ゴウライ
#. de: Gorai der Entfesselte
#. fr: Gôrai le fureteur
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: The ruin of the man once known as Gorai, head monk of the venerated Shojo Temple. An avid collector, his attachment to the many rare treasures in his possession served only to stoke the flames of his avarice─until naught of the man he was remained.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:379:0:0"
msgid "Gorai the Uncaged"
msgstr "Горай Непокорный"

