#. de: Shishio
#. fr: Shishiô
#. column 0: Shishio
#. column 8: A mythical beast feared in Hingashi since the days of yore, this creature figures in over one hundred legends. While some believe it to be the king of the nue, others insist it is a manifestation of fear itself, born from the quavering hearts of men who have heard the cries that reverberate amongst the mountains of Shishu at night.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:384:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: ひんがしの国において、古来より畏れられてきた大怪異。瑞獣ヌエの王と語られるが、その伝承は多彩であり、ゆうに百を超える。夜山に響く不気味な物音に対する恐怖心が実体化したものであると主張する者もいるようだ。
#. de: In Hingashi ranken sich zahlreiche Legenden um dieses Wesen, wobei die Gängigste besagt, dass es sich um den König der löwenähnlichen Nue handeln solle. Einer anderen Legende zufolge ist es die Manifestation der Furcht vor den schauerlichen Geräuschen des nächtlichen Berges.
#. fr: Une mythique créature crainte en Hingashi depuis les temps anciens. Les légendes à son sujet sont multiples, mais la plus communément racontée veut que Shishiô soit le roi des chimères. Pour certains, il serait l'incarnation de la peur des habitants de Shishû la nuit venue, lorsque d'inquétants râles se font entendre dans les montagnes...
#. column 0: Shishio
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:384:0:8"
msgid "A mythical beast feared in Hingashi since the days of yore, this creature figures in over one hundred legends. While some believe it to be the king of the nue, others insist it is a manifestation of fear itself, born from the quavering hearts of men who have heard the cries that reverberate amongst the mountains of Shishu at night."
msgstr "Это мифическое чудовище издревле внушает страх жителям Хингаси и упоминается более чем в сотне легенд. Одни считают его царём нуэ, другие — воплощением самого страха, рождённым трепещущими сердцами тех, кто слышал ночные крики в горах Сисю."

#. ja: テミス
#. de: Themis
#. fr: Thémis
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “And among these uncountable stars, it was yours that crossed my path. For that I shall be forever grateful.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:385:0:0"
msgid "Themis"
msgstr "Фемид"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Themis
#. fr: Thémis
#. column 0: Themis
#. column 8: “And among these uncountable stars, it was yours that crossed my path. For that I shall be forever grateful.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:385:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「数多の星のどれでもない。<br>君という星が私の前に現れたことを、幸福に思う」<br>古き助言者：テミス
#. de: „Kein Stern ist wie der andere<nbsp>... Ich bin wirklich glücklich, dass ich dein Funkeln sehen durfte.“
#. fr: “Je remercie le destin d'avoir mis sur mon chemin une étoile à nulle autre pareille. Je veux évidemment parler de toi.”
#. column 0: Themis
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:385:0:8"
msgid "“And among these uncountable stars, it was yours that crossed my path. For that I shall be forever grateful.”"
msgstr "«Среди бесчисленных звёзд именно твоя пересекла мой путь. И за это я буду вечно благодарен»"

#. ja: 煙々羅
#. de: Enenra
#. fr: Enenra
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This tsukumogami arose from a pipe said to grant its owner joy or sorrow according to its whims─though the fates of those that once possessed it seem curiously amenable to either interpretation, depending on who tells the tale. Perhaps that is why it takes the form of smoke, shrouding that which mortal eyes are so desperate to see laid bare.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:386:0:0"
msgid "Enenra"
msgstr "Энэнра"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Enenra
#. fr: Enenra
#. column 0: Enenra
#. column 8: This tsukumogami arose from a pipe said to grant its owner joy or sorrow according to its whims─though the fates of those that once possessed it seem curiously amenable to either interpretation, depending on who tells the tale. Perhaps that is why it takes the form of smoke, shrouding that which mortal eyes are so desperate to see laid bare.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:386:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 持ち主を幸福に、あるいは不幸にするという、相反したいわくがある大煙管に宿った付喪神。だが、結局は幸も不幸も考え方次第。結末に理由を求める人々の想いを煙に巻くかのように、その付喪神は変幻自在に立ち回るという。
#. de: Sowohl Glück als auch Pech vermag dieser eine Pfeife beseelende Tsukumo-Kami seinem Gebieter zu bringen. Doch hängen Glück und Pech nicht immer ganz von der Betrachtungsweise der Dinge ab? Die Gefühle all jener, die nach einem Grund für alles Geschehene suchen, sind der Nährboden für die Wandlungsfähigkeit dieses Kami.
#. fr: L'esprit divin habitant la grande pipe sacrée, capable selon la légende d'apporter bonheur ou malheur à son pro<shy>prié<shy>taire. Il a le pouvoir de transformer son apparence à loisir, comme pour noyer dans la fumée les pensées de ceux qui espèrent trouver une explication à leur destinée.
#. column 0: Enenra
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:386:0:8"
msgid "This tsukumogami arose from a pipe said to grant its owner joy or sorrow according to its whims─though the fates of those that once possessed it seem curiously amenable to either interpretation, depending on who tells the tale. Perhaps that is why it takes the form of smoke, shrouding that which mortal eyes are so desperate to see laid bare."
msgstr "Этот цукумогами появился из большой трубки, которой, по слухам, досталась власть приносить хозяину то радость, то горе. Судьбу её прежних владельцев и вправду можно истолковать и так и этак — смотря кто рассказывает. Быть может, потому дух и принимает облик дыма, скрывая от смертных глаз то, что им так отчаянно хочется увидеть."

#. ja: ゴルベーザ
#. de: Golbez
#. fr: Golbez
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Leader of the four archfiends, this enigmatic knight in black marshaled a great host of voidsent in a campaign of conquest in the Thirteenth. Once his supremacy was established, Golbez's focus turned to his true ambition: invading the aether-rich world of the Source.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:387:0:0"
msgid "Golbez"
msgstr "Голбез"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Golbez
#. fr: Golbez
#. column 0: Golbez
#. column 8: Leader of the four archfiends, this enigmatic knight in black marshaled a great host of voidsent in a campaign of conquest in the Thirteenth. Once his supremacy was established, Golbez's focus turned to his true ambition: invading the aether-rich world of the Source.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:387:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 謎多き黒鎧の騎士。四天王と呼ばれる四体の大妖異を筆頭に数多くの配下を引き連れ、いくつもの領域を蹂躙し、ヴォイドにおいて勢力を拡大させていた。その目的は、原初世界への侵攻であったようだが……。
#. de: Geheimnisvoller Ritter in schwarzer Rüstung und Anführer von vier mächtigen Nichtswesen, die als die vier Elementarfürsten bekannt geworden sind. Mit einer gewaltigen Zahl an Vasallen überrannte er ein Reich nach dem anderen und vergrößerte seine Macht über das Nichts. Sein Ziel war die Ursprungs<shy>welt, doch sein Schicksal war der Tod.
#. fr: Maître incontesté des forces du néant, à commencer par ses quatre fidèles généraux, ce mystérieux chevalier en armure noire s'est juré d'offrir une vie meilleure à son peuple déchu. Il semblerait pour cela ambitionner d'envahir le monde primitif...
#. column 0: Golbez
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:387:0:8"
msgid "Leader of the four archfiends, this enigmatic knight in black marshaled a great host of voidsent in a campaign of conquest in the Thirteenth. Once his supremacy was established, Golbez's focus turned to his true ambition: invading the aether-rich world of the Source."
msgstr "Загадочный рыцарь в чёрных доспехах, предводитель четырёх архизверей. Собрав огромное войско пустотников, он повёл их завоёвывать Тринадцатый. Утвердив там свою власть, Голбез обратился к истинной цели — вторжению в Исток, мир, богатый эфиром."

#. ja: アテナ
#. de: Athena
#. fr: Athéna
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Pandæmonium's first chief keyward, Athena used a man named Claudien as a vessel to house her memories, traversing eons and coming within an ilm of godhood. Luckily for the whole star, her ambitions were cut short before they could be realized.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:388:0:0"
msgid "Athena"
msgstr "Афина"

