msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 初代パンデモニウム長官、アテナの記憶がクローディエンという「神の原型」を得ることで顕現した超越的存在。魂を自在に生み出す「神」たらんとしたが、あと一歩のところで、冒険者によって野望を阻止された。
#. de: Eine Existenz, die sich aus den Erinnerungen der Direktorin des ersten Pandæmoniums und Professor Claudien als geeignete Form manifestierte. Athena wollte sich zur Gottheit emporschwingen und nach Belieben Seelen erschaffen, aber ihre ehrgeizigen Pläne wurden glück<shy>licher<shy>weise vereitelt.
#. fr: Ancienne directrice du Pandæmonium, Athéna s'est servie du professeur Claudien comme réceptacle de ses souvenirs, ceci afin d'accéder au rang de déesse créatrice. Mais elle fut stoppée par <if $gn4>la Guerrière<else>le Guerrier</if> de la Lumière avant de parvenir à ses fins.
#. column 0: Athena
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:388:0:8"
msgid "Pandæmonium's first chief keyward, Athena used a man named Claudien as a vessel to house her memories, traversing eons and coming within an ilm of godhood. Luckily for the whole star, her ambitions were cut short before they could be realized."
msgstr "Афина, первая глава Пандемониума, использовала мужчину по имени Клодиен как сосуд для своих воспоминаний. Пережив целые эпохи, она приблизилась к божественности, но, к счастью для всей звезды, её амбиции пресекли прежде, чем они воплотились в жизнь."

#. ja: ケトゥドゥケ
#. de: Ketuduke
#. fr: Ketuduke
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Legends of the south sea isles tell of whales that soar through the heavens. Shockmaw is spoken of in hushed whispers, but on the island of Aloalo a creature named “Ketuduke” was an object of reverence. Believed to be a divine messenger, Ketuduke would descend from the skies on a night when the winds howled and waters raged. The faithful would then climb atop its back and be delivered to paradise.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:389:0:0"
msgid "Ketuduke"
msgstr "Кетудуке"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Ketuduke
#. fr: Ketuduke
#. column 0: Ketuduke
#. column 8: Legends of the south sea isles tell of whales that soar through the heavens. Shockmaw is spoken of in hushed whispers, but on the island of Aloalo a creature named “Ketuduke” was an object of reverence. Believed to be a divine messenger, Ketuduke would descend from the skies on a night when the winds howled and waters raged. The faithful would then climb atop its back and be delivered to paradise.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:389:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: アロアロ島で遭遇した海洋生物。南洋諸島には「ショックモー」をはじめとする空飛ぶクジラ伝説が残っているが、ケトゥドゥケもそのひとつ。曰く、神の使いであり、古き水と風の夜、善き人々を背に乗せ新天地へ導いたという。
#. de: In den Sagen und Legenden der südlichen Inseln kommen fliegende Walfische häufig vor, und neben Schockschlund ist Ketuduke ein prominenter Vertreter. Es heißt, dass er ein Bote der Götter ist, und jene mit reinem Herzen in einer ganz bestimmten Nacht auf seinem Rücken in eine neue Welt trug.
#. fr: Une baleine volante légendaire des îles méridionales, connue aussi sous le nom de “choc-gueule”. Selon la tradition locale, elle serait une envoyée des dieux, chargée de transporter les vertueux vers une nouvelle terre fertile.
#. column 0: Ketuduke
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:389:0:8"
msgid "Legends of the south sea isles tell of whales that soar through the heavens. Shockmaw is spoken of in hushed whispers, but on the island of Aloalo a creature named “Ketuduke” was an object of reverence. Believed to be a divine messenger, Ketuduke would descend from the skies on a night when the winds howled and waters raged. The faithful would then climb atop its back and be delivered to paradise."
msgstr "Легенды южных островов рассказывают о китах, парящих в небесах. Об Удароклыке говорят шёпотом, а на острове Алоало почитали существо по имени Кетудуке. Считалось, что оно — посланник богов и спускается с небес в ночь, когда воют ветра и бушуют воды. Тогда верующие взбирались ему на спину, и оно уносило их в рай."

#. ja: ララ
#. de: Lala
#. fr: Lala
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Encountered on Aloalo Island, the lala's wooden construction sets it apart from the stone frames of other golems. Derived from the esoteric mathematics that formed the basis of arcanima, the geometries carved into its surface enable complex and adaptive defensive measures.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:390:0:0"
msgid "Lala"
msgstr "Лала"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Lala
#. fr: Lala
#. column 0: Lala
#. column 8: Encountered on Aloalo Island, the lala's wooden construction sets it apart from the stone frames of other golems. Derived from the esoteric mathematics that formed the basis of arcanima, the geometries carved into its surface enable complex and adaptive defensive measures.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:390:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: アロアロ島で遭遇した守護像。通常、この種のゴーレムは耐久性に優れた石材を用いて造られるが、ララは木材によって構築されている。どうやら巴術の源流たる「算術」の産物らしく、魔紋による複雑な制御機構を備えているのも特徴的。
#. de: Dieser Golem wacht über Aloalo. Normalerweise werden solche Exemplare aus hartem Stein gebaut, aber Lala ist gänzlich aus Holz gefertigt. Er scheint ein Produkt der Zahlenlehre und damit der Wiege der Hermetik zu sein, und zeichnet sich durch seinen Umgang mit komplexen Äthergrammen aus.
#. fr: Cette statue animée est le gardien de l'arbre géant au centre d'Aloalo. Habituellement, les golems de ce type sont construits en pierre, mais Lala est constitué de bois. Créé grâce aux arithméticiens et à leur art à l'origine de l'arcanisme moderne, il se caractérise également par son mécanisme de contrôle complexe utilisant des cercles magiques.
#. column 0: Lala
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:390:0:8"
msgid "Encountered on Aloalo Island, the lala's wooden construction sets it apart from the stone frames of other golems. Derived from the esoteric mathematics that formed the basis of arcanima, the geometries carved into its surface enable complex and adaptive defensive measures."
msgstr "На острове Алоало встретился этот деревянный голем — в отличие от прочих, чьи тела вырезаны из камня. В его основе лежит эзотерическая математика, на которой строится арканима. Геометрические узоры на поверхности позволяют ему применять сложную и гибкую защиту."

#. ja: スターチス
#. de: Statice
#. fr: Statice
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This mischievous faerie was left behind by her masters, but even after their deaths, her aether did not dissipate. After countless years of solitude, Statice's once congenial personality warped into something much more wicked. Perhaps due to a sense of kinship with other lost things, she makes ingenious use of items collected from shipwrecks and other detritus that washes ashore.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:391:0:0"
msgid "Statice"
msgstr "Статице"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Statice
#. fr: Statice
#. column 0: Statice
#. column 8: This mischievous faerie was left behind by her masters, but even after their deaths, her aether did not dissipate. After countless years of solitude, Statice's once congenial personality warped into something much more wicked. Perhaps due to a sense of kinship with other lost things, she makes ingenious use of items collected from shipwrecks and other detritus that washes ashore.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:391:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: いたずら好きのはぐれフェアリー。主の死後もエーテルが霧散せず、以後の長い時を孤独に彷徨ってきた。本質的には人が好きなのだが、その接し方には問題が多い。難破船の積荷や漂着物から集めた品々を使って、歪んだ愛情を表現するだろう。
#. de: Statice hat sich nach dem Tod ihres Meisters nicht in Äther aufgelöst und haust seither alleine auf Aloalo. Sie ist neugierig und freundlich, was den Umgang mit Besuchern betrifft, allerdings hapert es daran, diese Freundlichkeit angemessen zu zeigen. Dabei möchte sie nur ihre liebsten Schätze aus ihren vielen Fundsachen teilen.
#. fr: Fée errante et espiègle, son éther ne s'est jamais dissipé après la mort de son maître, et elle a longtemps erré seule depuis. Elle aime beaucoup les gens, mais sa manière d'interagir avec eux laisse énormément à désirer. Pour oublier sa solitude, elle s'est prise de passion pour les objets récupérés sur les épaves de bateau jonchant la côte d'Aloalo.
#. column 0: Statice
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:391:0:8"
msgid "This mischievous faerie was left behind by her masters, but even after their deaths, her aether did not dissipate. After countless years of solitude, Statice's once congenial personality warped into something much more wicked. Perhaps due to a sense of kinship with other lost things, she makes ingenious use of items collected from shipwrecks and other detritus that washes ashore."
msgstr "Эту проказливую фею бросили хозяева, но даже после их смерти её эфир не рассеялся. За бесчисленные годы одиночества её приветливый нрав исказился, и она стала куда злее. Быть может, чувствуя родство с прочими потеряшками, Статице ловко пускает в ход вещи, найденные среди обломков кораблей и прочего мусора, выброшенного на берег."

#. ja: コヨコヨ
#. de: Koyo-Koyo
#. fr: Koyo K
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: “PuPu... I hail...PuPuPuPu...from a star...PuPu...a great distance from here.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:392:0:0"
msgid "PuPu"
msgstr "Пу-Пу"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Koyo-Koyo
#. fr: Koyo K
#. column 0: PuPu
#. column 8: “PuPu... I hail...PuPuPuPu...from a star...PuPu...a great distance from here.”
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:392:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 「コヨコヨ……ボクは……コヨコヨコヨ……<br>遠い星から……コヨコヨ……やってきた」<br>異星のトモダチ：コヨコヨ
#. de: Koyo-Koyo. Ich<nbsp>... Koyo-Koyo<nbsp>... von einem<nbsp>... Koyo-Koyo<nbsp>... gekommen.<br>Dein Freund von einem anderen Stern: Koyo-Koyo
#. fr: “Koyo-koyo... je viens... koyo... d'une étoile... koyo-koyo... lointaine.”
#. column 0: PuPu
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:392:0:8"
msgid "“PuPu... I hail...PuPuPuPu...from a star...PuPu...a great distance from here.”"
msgstr "«Пу-Пу... Я... Пу-Пу-Пу-Пу... прибыл с далёкой... Пу-Пу... звезды»"

#. ja: ロクロクイ
#. de: Loquloqui
#. fr: Loquloqui
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: This statue and the shrine which houses it were built by the forgotten people of the south sea isles. It is presumed that the figure represents a teller of prophecy, but there are no records to illuminate the faith of its builders. Newer arrivals to Aloalo came to revere the figure, calling it “she who speaks and is spoken to”─or “Speaker,” as Kalika so succinctly translates.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:393:0:0"
msgid "Loquloqui"
msgstr "Локулоки"

#. ja: 0
#. de: 0
#. fr: Loquloqui
#. column 0: Loquloqui
#. column 8: This statue and the shrine which houses it were built by the forgotten people of the south sea isles. It is presumed that the figure represents a teller of prophecy, but there are no records to illuminate the faith of its builders. Newer arrivals to Aloalo came to revere the figure, calling it “she who speaks and is spoken to”─or “Speaker,” as Kalika so succinctly translates.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:393:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: アロアロ島に祀られていた「忘れられた人々」の神子像。おそらく、託宣を伝える神子を象ったものと推測される。しかし、いかなる信仰であったのか記録はなく、後年、島にやって来た者たちは、「相談され、語る者」を示す名で呼んで尊んだという。
#. de: Die „Vergessenen“, die vor langer Zeit auf Aloalo hausten, schufen diese riesige Holzstatue. Es wird vermutet, dass sie ein prophetisches Orakel darstellt, allerdings gibt es keinerlei Auf<shy>zeich<shy>nun<shy>gen über diesen Glauben. Später wurde die Statue als „die Sprecherin“ verehrt und auf den gleichbedeutenden Namen Loquloqui getauft.
#. fr: La statue de la prêtresse du “peuple oublié” laissée sur l'île d'Aloalo. Les historiens supposent qu'elle représente une figure religieuse, comme un oracle, mais aucune trace ne permet d'attester de la foi qui régissait l'île à l'époque. Les habitants arrivés par la suite lui ont affublé son nom, signifiant “celle qui est consultée et qui transmet”.
#. column 0: Loquloqui
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:393:0:8"
msgid "This statue and the shrine which houses it were built by the forgotten people of the south sea isles. It is presumed that the figure represents a teller of prophecy, but there are no records to illuminate the faith of its builders. Newer arrivals to Aloalo came to revere the figure, calling it “she who speaks and is spoken to”─or “Speaker,” as Kalika so succinctly translates."
msgstr "Эту статую и святилище, где она хранится, построили забытый народ южных островов. Полагают, что фигура изображает прорицательницу, но сведений о вере её создателей не сохранилось. Позднее прибывшие на Алоало стали почитать её и назвали «той, что говорит и к которой обращаются», или, как коротко перевёл Калика, «Говорящей»."

#. ja: ノフィカ
#. de: Nophica
#. fr: Nophica
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Tender of soils and harvests and goddess of abundance, Nophica is often depicted as a jubilant farmer holding a scythe of steel. She is greatly revered in Gridania, and the deity's more warlike incarnation famously graces a recruitment poster for the Order of the Twin Adder. Although mythological tales put her at odds with Halone, the Fury, the two seemed to bear each other no ill will in Euphrosyne.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:394:0:0"
msgid "Nophica"
msgstr "Нофика"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Nophica
#. fr: Nophica
#. column 0: Nophica
#. column 8: Tender of soils and harvests and goddess of abundance, Nophica is often depicted as a jubilant farmer holding a scythe of steel. She is greatly revered in Gridania, and the deity's more warlike incarnation famously graces a recruitment poster for the Order of the Twin Adder. Although mythological tales put her at odds with Halone, the Fury, the two seemed to bear each other no ill will in Euphrosyne.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:394:0:2"
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#. ja: 大地と豊穣を司る女神。鋼の大鎌を持つ陽気な農民の姿で描かれることが多い。森都では特に厚く信仰され、双蛇党の募兵ポスターにおける姿も有名。なお、戦神ハルオーネとの不仲を描いた神話も伝わるが、少なくとも神域においてその様子はなかった。
#. de: Sie ist die Göttin des Bodens und der Fruchtbarkeit. In der Kunst wird sie oft als muntere Bäuerin mit stählerner Sense dargestellt. Unter der Bevölkerung der Wälder Gridanias ist sie anscheinend so beliebt, dass ihr Antlitz die Rekrutierungsplakate der Bruderschaft der Morgenviper schmückt. Allerdings werden in manchen Mythen auch ihre Streitereien mit der Göttin des Krieges, Halone, beschrieben. Zumindest im Schemenreich gibt es jedoch keinerlei Hinweise hierzu.
#. fr: Déesse de la fertilité et gardienne des sols et des cultures, elle est généralement représentée sous la forme d'une paysanne joyeuse portant une faux d'acier. Protectrice de Gridania, elle est révérée par l'ordre des Deux Vipères qui la fait figurer en bonne place sur ses affiches de recrutement. Les récits mythologiques mentionnent souvent sa relation conflictuelle avec Halone, mais dans le domaine divin, rien ne semblait prouver cette croyance.
#. column 0: Nophica
#. column 2: 0
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:394:0:8"
msgid "Tender of soils and harvests and goddess of abundance, Nophica is often depicted as a jubilant farmer holding a scythe of steel. She is greatly revered in Gridania, and the deity's more warlike incarnation famously graces a recruitment poster for the Order of the Twin Adder. Although mythological tales put her at odds with Halone, the Fury, the two seemed to bear each other no ill will in Euphrosyne."
msgstr "Нофика — богиня плодородия, покровительница земли и урожая. Её часто изображают весёлой крестьянкой с железной косой. В Гридании её особенно почитают, а её воинственный образ знаком всем по плакатам Ордена Двух Змей. В мифах Нофика враждует с Халон, Фурией, но в Эвфросине они, похоже, не питали друг к другу неприязни."

#. ja: アルジク
#. de: Althyk
#. fr: Althyk
#. column 2: 0
#. column 8: Althyk is the god of time and the surveyor of change and space. He commands the element of earth, and is most often depicted as an austere emperor wielding a mythril greataxe. Said to be the first of the Twelve, his presence in Euphrosyne is one characterized by quiet authority, though he seems much softened in dealings with his younger sister, Nymeia.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:395:0:0"
msgid "Althyk"
msgstr "Алтек"

#. ja: 0
#. de: Althyk
#. fr: Althyk
#. column 0: Althyk
#. column 8: Althyk is the god of time and the surveyor of change and space. He commands the element of earth, and is most often depicted as an austere emperor wielding a mythril greataxe. Said to be the first of the Twelve, his presence in Euphrosyne is one characterized by quiet authority, though he seems much softened in dealings with his younger sister, Nymeia.
msgctxt "TripleTriadCard:395:0:2"
